font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/7naozg4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T01:11:06-07:00","id":1065131,"title":"","content":"Chapter 4 \u2013 Reunion under the best of circumstances<br /> <br /> Riley fled town on foot, trekking cross-country to the Lawson farm. They avoided the humans on the property, made their way to the building where Terah was stabled, and curled up in a corner of the horse\u2019s stall.<br /> <br /> Elsie sat quietly in the room as she listened to the Reverend describe his assault at Riley\u2019s hands. The sheriff, an older man with a mane of white hair, listened gravely. She perked up when she realised they were talking about Riley. \u201cHey, that\u2019s my friend!\u201d<br /> <br /> Abram returned to the house with Al, to find the place turned upside down by Elsie\u2019s cleaning efforts. Al seemed more bemused than upset. When Abram asked permission to leave and track down \u201cthe wife\u201d, Al waved him off.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust be back here in the afternoon. We\u2019re going to pay our friend a visit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Abram eventually located Elsie. She was wandering around Main Street, gawping at the different shops. When he asked her where she\u2019d been, the whole story of running into Riley, then meeting the priest, then meeting the sheriff, then the sheriff agreeing to hunt Riley, then her telling him how she was looking for Riley too, then him asking her to leave while he went about his business, then her coming to Main Street to look at the markets, then how she ran into Abram came tumbling out. Abram wasn\u2019t given a chance to interrupt as the words burbled happily over him. When she finally stopped because she\u2019d recounted everything up to the present, he took a deep breath and tried to get as much information as he could out of her. He worked out where she\u2019d seen Riley from the clues Elsie had bothered to remember, and even roughly what direction Riley had been heading in. There didn\u2019t seem to be any chance of finding Riley by searching on foot, but Abram hoped he could at least stop the Sheriff from intervening. He went back to Al\u2019s home, got a pen and paper together, and he and Elsie wrote a letter to the Sheriff asking him to please not hurt their friend.<br /> <br /> On the Lawson farm, Riley\u2019s miserable reverie was slowly intruded on by the sounds of a commotion emanating from the family home. They could hear voices coming from far off and near, all calling out a single name. \u201cMary! Mary!\u201d<br /> <br /> They shook themselves free of their misery long enough to go outside. Jarred was standing there, looking shocked to see Riley emerge from the stables. He\u2019d been in and out all day, but Riley had kept out of sight. But he was also distracted, and didn\u2019t waste time asking what Riley was doing there. When Riley asked what the commotion was, Jarred explained that his niece, Mary, was missing. Riley joined the search, going off on their own, seeing what tracks they could find.<br /> <br /> It took them a few hours, but they found the young girl\u2019s tracks leading towards town. Riley eventually found her sitting in the lee of a rock, some distance from the road. She was filthy and looked absolutely miserable. Not sure how to approach the situation, Riley stood somewhere where they were plainly visible and waved. When the girl made no effort to come closer, Riley tentatively advanced. The girl stood up, and Riley froze in place. At last, Riley spoke, telling the girl that her parents were worried and looking for her. She stared at her feet at that, and told them that she didn\u2019t want to go back. Her family was cursed. They were poor, their animals and crops kept dying, her parents were never happy, she was never happy. But she was lost and tired and hungry and she wasn\u2019t too hard to persuade to get onto Terah\u2019s back and allow Riley to lead her back to the farm.<br /> <br /> Back in town, Al and Abram got into Al\u2019s car, joined by two local boys who\u2019d agreed to help. They drove north from the town, reaching a farm that looked like it had fallen upon hard times. There was no one in the farmhouse when they knocked, but they could see figures out in the fields. One of those figures came towards them, a lean young man with a worried expression.<br /> <br /> \u201cTime\u2019s up, Jack. Time to pay,\u201d Al said, sounding almost bored.<br /> <br /> The man protested. His daughter was missing. Once he found her he\u2019d be able to get the money together. If Al would just come back in a few days\u2019 time\u2026<br /> <br /> Al gave Abram a look, one Abram knew the meaning of. He stepped forward. Jack clearly recognised the danger. He threw a punch at Abram. Even though the Tammuz made no effort to dodge the blow, the wild swing still went wide. Then Abram slammed his fist into the base of Jack\u2019s jaw. Something crunched. He staggered, slipped to one knee. Half a broken tooth fell from his lips, a thin trail of blood with it. Then Abram was on top of the farmer, bearing him down to the ground, pinning his arms easily.<br /> <br /> Al whistled, and his two helpers came out of the car. He sent them towards one of the barns, and they soon emerged carrying bits and pieces that Abram recognised from a still. Once they had removed everything the car would carry, they went back inside one last time. Abram could hear glass breaking, loud bangs, as whatever else was in there was systematically destroyed. Jack mumbled pleas through his bloody lips. The bank would repossess the farm if they didn\u2019t make the next repayment. His family would be homeless. Al didn\u2019t seem to be listening.<br /> <br /> At last, the men emerged. Al looked down at Jack and sighed. \u201cSorry about this, Jack,\u201d he said, and kicked the man in the head. Jack went limp. Al walked back towards the car, and Abram dutifully followed. They drove away.<br /> <br /> A horrified Riley slumped against the wall of the main farmhouse. They\u2019d been watching everything, keeping Mary out of sight where she couldn\u2019t see. At last they stepped out, carrying Mary, in time to see Jarred and the woman they assumed was Jarred\u2019s sister, Jack\u2019s wife, come rushing up. The woman, Maureen, was too distracted by her husband\u2019s injury to pay much attention to their return. She made sure Jack was still breathing, then tried to help him up. <br /> <br /> Then Jarred spotted the open barn door. He rushed to it, swung it open. When he saw the destruction inside he threw his head back and howled.<br /> <br /> Riley let Mary run to her mother. They stared at the tableau.<br /> <br /> \u201cBe better,\u201d they said quietly to the stunned family. And then they left.<br /> <br /> Although Riley felt the temptation to seek out the source of their vision from the Athanor, the place of pale leaves and still water, they couldn\u2019t let things with Abram stand like this. They stuck to the outskirts of Joseph\u2019s Cross, wandering until they found the car they\u2019d seen up at the Lawson farm. They saw Al saying goodbye to Abram, and then driving off. Abram went back inside the house.<br /> <br /> Riley approached the building. They checked the windows, spotting Elsie inside as well, but no humans. They went to the front door and knocked. <br /> <br /> The following hour was long, almost excruciatingly so. The throng was wounded, Abram and Riley each felt aggrieved by the other\u2019s actions. Abram felt Riley had no right to criticise the recent violence, when it had been committed so that the throng would have somewhere to stay and look for Riley. He was able to explain, finally, that the pain Riley had suffered was unintended. And when it was clear that Riley was still hurt, he offered to go out and look for someone to care for them. He wanted to help. He had always just wanted to help.<br /> <br /> Riley, for their part, was struggling with guilt at having behaved so much like Malik. They recounted what had happened to them since they had left the group, and described the visions they\u2019d had of the pale leaves. They told Abram to go and look for Iris, since she had been the one who had cared for them originally, and she had mentioned she was a gardener. She might know something.<br /> <br /> Abram went to look, since it wasn\u2019t safe for Riley to be wandering the streets with the Sheriff looking for them. They ask around and are able to find Iris\u2019s house. They pass Sarah Lawson\u2019s dress shop, and see the Sheriff inside speaking to her.<br /> <br /> Iris, for her part, is happy to come. All Abram tells her is that he is from out of town, and that his child is hurt. When they arrive at the house and step inside, she is surprised to see Riley. She starts to care for them, and tells them that they need to stay put for the next few days in order to completely heal.<br /> <br /> As she works, Riley asks her about the plant. As they describe it, Iris begins to look worried. She asks them where they heard of it, and Riley lies and says that the priest spoke of it. This seems to concern Iris even more. She looks at the other two Prometheans, and tells Riley that, although she likes them, she isn\u2019t sure if she can trust their family. Riley persuades her otherwise, telling her how far out of their way their family had come to look for them.<br /> <br /> At last, Iris agrees. \u201cWhen you are healed, I will take you to the plant you described,\u201d she says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T01:21:14-07:00","id":1065134,"title":"","content":"A few quick notes I didn't really find a good way to weave into the story:<br /> <br /> Mary Lawson is at Disquiet Level 1, because Riley's player is just so darn good at rolling Disquiet checks.<br /> <br /> Riley completed the Watcher Role when they decided not to get involved in the Abram/Al vs Jack Lawson dispute. They haven't yet settled on a new role or the new Alembics they've unlocked, but I'll make some note of it when they do.<br /> <br /> I glossed over a loooot of the conversation between Riley and Abram, but this was basically the heart of the session. One of the things I most regret about this way of recapping the game is that I can't quite capture that kind of back-and-forth roleplay very well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So much drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:25:16-07:00","id":1069819,"title":"","content":"Chapter 5 \u2013 The Root of the Problem<br /> <br /> Riley took a few days before they felt fully recovered from their wounds. Iris visited every day, checking on their progress. She didn't talk much, but she didn't show any visible signs of suffering from Disquiet.<br /> <br /> On the Sunday, Elsie attended the church service out of curiosity. The Reverend seemed pleased to see her there, though a little wary after the revelation that she was friends with Riley, but the two didn't spend much time talking. Afterwards she wandered around town for a while, but all the stores were shut and she ended up back at the house. The following day she picked up the new clothes for Baby.<br /> <br /> Iris had deemed Riley fit earlier that morning. She came back in the evening and led the throng to a hill outside of Joseph's Cross. There were a group of figures, hard to make out in the darkness, waiting for them when they arrived. It wasn't until they were almost face to face that Abram and Elsie recognised the Sheriff. Abram tensed, but Iris hurried to make clear that they meant no harm. The sheriff, and those with him, were locals who knew of the plant the characters had described. She beckoned them to follow her, and parted the long, hanging grass on the hill to reveal a deep passage, tall enough for even Abram to walk down without stooping. Just inside where was a small sign nailed to the wall. &quot;Sioc's Cavern&quot;.<br /> <br /> The group descended into the depths of Sioc\u2019s Cavern. Iris spoke to Riley, telling them of how she found this place. She described how Joseph's Cross had been devastated by the onset of the Dust Bowl, the first Black Blizzard several years ago had almost destroyed it. Her own home\u2019s roof caved in. Her husband was shattered and left her in the aftermath. Then she heard the voice one day while trying to coax life back into her garden. The voice, named, Sioc told her what she needed to do to restore the fortunes of the town.<br /> <br /> As the rocky entrance gave way to a maze of slick clay walls and damp air, the sheriff further back in the line mentioned to Elsie and Abram that he had got her letter asking him to show mercy to Riley. Elsie found this enormously gratifying.<br /> <br /> The twists and turns the throng had to follow quickly made it clear that it would have been easy to get lost without Iris as their guide. At last the tunnels gave way to a cavern. The circle of light from their guides' torches didn't illuminate very far, but they could see a large pool of water running almost to the cavern's entrance. It was clear and shallow, hardly more than ankle height. Iris's decision to wear wellingtons became a bit more clear, as she strode forward into the pool. The flickering light of her torch soon illuminated a tangled mass of vines sporting large, pale leaves. The leaves dipped low to the water, as if drinking it.<br /> <br /> Riley opened their eyes to Twilight, and found that the plant existed both there and in the real world. They looked back and saw that their water spirit companion was coiled at the entrance to the cavern, refusing to come closer to the plant. They stepped forward, took a deep breath, and reached out to one of the leaves. When they touched it their muscles locked in place. Though to Abram and Elsie it looked like Riley was just, just barely brushing their fingertips across the leaves, Riley felt utterly paralysed. And then they felt a sibilant voice slide into their mind.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you wish?\u201d<br /> <br /> Riley's thoughts filled with Malik, their need to find him, their desire to find out where he had gone.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what are you willing to pay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Riley's first thoughts were of their Pyros, but Sioc\u2019s revulsion was immediate and clear. It hissed into their mind about its hatred for such burning, twisting change. Riley's muscles trembled, but they didn't lose contact with the plant. They thought then of their physical possessions, but Sioc gave the mental equivalent of a yawn. It had no interest in such things. Finally, Riley considered the ephemera in their bodies in place of blood, and Sioc was intrigued. It asked for a taste, and in return it would show them what they wanted. Riley asked for a moment to speak to the others, and Sioc generously allowed it.<br /> <br /> It took a few minutes for the Prometheans to come a decision. Abram didn't like the idea of Riley being hurt by this thing. Iris was standing nearby so he couldn't express his true feelings, but he desperately wanted to bring the entire cavern crashing down.<br /> <br /> Riley couldn't be dissuaded. They stepped back to Sioc to let the creature know and found their hand plunging onto one of the thorns and dragging, carving a deep, long furrow in their flesh. No ectoplasm gushed from the wound, every drop was pulled into Sioc.<br /> <br /> In the midst of the sudden loss of essence they saw in their mind's eye a vision of Malik rushing into the church, his right arm smoking. They heard a sound like a pack of hunting dogs. They could dimly hear Sioc\u2019s voice saying that after that night, Malik fled north and beyond Sioc's sight, leaving corruption in his wake. When Riley\u2019s eyes opened they realised from the Vitriol in their veins that the Jovian Athanor has been resolved.<br /> <br /> Iris's eyes clouded and she started to speak with a voice that Riley recognised as having echoes of Sioc's. She told them that their caustic presence would undo the good work Sioc had worked upon Joseph's Cross. They were ordered to leave town in the next 24 hours.<br /> <br /> They are led from the cave and head back to town. Riley wanted to make sure they had investigated the matter of the ghost in the graveyard before they left Joseph's Cross. The throng headed to the graveyard, where they waited until past midnight for the spectre to appear. The young black man appeared in the same place as before, beneath the broken bough of the graveyard's only tree. The rope around his neck trailed behind him as he ran towards the church.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans, who had hidden within the graveyard, rushed in to talk to the ghost. He pushed past them, pausing only when Riley grabbed him. He had materialised physically, but was uninterested in conversation. His only words were cries for mercy. Abram grunted and clasped at his head, feeling a cavalcade of images and sensations fill his mind. He was being beaten, burnt, hung. He choked and gagged. The ghost struggles against Riley who, rather than hold on, chose to release him. Abram staggered upright and the Prometheans followed him into the church. Riley stayed at the door as the others headed inside.<br /> <br /> The ghost rushed to the altar, hands reaching out for it. Just before they made contact his body froze, and Abram and Elsie could see his flesh indent and his clothes bunch in places moments before he was hurled to the ground by invisible hands. He curled into a ball and his body jerked and shuddered as if he was being kicked and beaten. In the midst of it his eyes fix on a place somewhere above him and he pleads, \u201cPlease, Sheriff.\u201d Then his eyes went wide and he vanished.<br /> <br /> The three Prometheans stood there in silence for some time. At last Abram told the others that they should go and pack and be ready to leave. When Riley turned to stare at him, he shrugged and said that when they confronted the Sheriff they would probably want to be able to get out of town quickly. <br /> <br /> They arrived at the Sheriff's home a few hours before dawn. Riley attempted to pick the lock, but their fumbling alerted the Sheriff. Riley and Abram hid when the door opened, to reveal the Sheriff with one hand hidden behind the door and obviously grasping a weapon. Elsie was left standing there in front of him. She smiled up at him disarmingly claimed that she just came by to say farewell. She asked him if he wanted to sit down for a cup of tea. The Sheriff stares at her beaming face for a moment, and then lets her inside.<br /> <br /> He was standing in the kitchen with his back turned to her when Elsie burned her Pyros and lashed at him with her Disquiet, forcing it into his mind. She charged him, trying to use that power to force him into submission, but he fended her off and struck her across the face. Elsie staggered, snarled, and leapt on him. The two were struggling when Riley and Abram rushed. Riley was carrying the sheriff\u2019s shotgun, left by the door. Pointing the weapon at him, with Elsie still hanging from his neck, they ordered him to freeze.<br /> <br /> Slowly, carefully, the Sheriff raised his hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:08:35-07:00","id":1072251,"title":"","content":"Alright. Two questions<br /> <br /> 1) are the baby and their donkeys gonna be infected by Disquiet?<br /> 2) what's a Jovian Athanor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:13:58-07:00","id":1072279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1072251#post1072251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. Two questions<br /> <br /> 1) are the baby and their donkeys gonna be infected by Disquiet?<br /> 2) what's a Jovian Athanor?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The baby and Terah, the horse, are not immune to Disquiet. Both are True Friends to their respective PCs though, so I've opted not to roll for Disquiet with them in most scenes, and give them a dice bonus when I do feel it's appropriate, but the narrative possibilities of either being infected with Disquiet are too awesome for me to rule that they'll be immune to Disquiet entirely.<br /> <br /> The idea of Baby being infected by Elsie's Disquiet is particularly disturbing, given how she inspires dark lust and possessiveness. So naturally we're going to have fun with that if the Baby ever fails a Disquiet check.<br /> <br /> 2) Jovian Athanors are a subset of Athanors made to dump negative persistent Conditions, and are generally tainted and have some kind of negative effect. In this case the Church's collection plate was holding Malik's Broken and Obsession Conditions, and its negative effect was that it leached Pyros from Prometheans on a touch. Taking on those Conditions and resolving them, as Riley did, resolves the Athanor and counts as a Milestone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:08:00-07:00","id":1073440,"title":"","content":"Chapter 6 \u2013 Outside the Law<br /> <br /> The Prometheans interrogated the Sheriff at gunpoint. They described the ghost in the graveyard, and said that they knew it was the Sheriff who killed him. It took a while before he even realised what they are talking about, and when he does finally did recognise the description he was more confused than anything. That was decades ago, he protested. How could they know anything about that?<br /> <br /> The Sheriff told them that race riots ripped through Joseph\u2019s Cross back in the 1910s. On this one particular night a mob, incited by the now-mayor, Meyer Kastern, decided to remove \u201ccriminal elements\u201d from the town that were a threat to their friends and families. The Sheriff claimed that his execution of the young man in the church was a mercy. If he hadn\u2019t shot him, he\u2019d have been torn limb from limb by the mob. Better a quick death.<br /> <br /> Abram and Riley had a quiet conversation and concluded that the Sheriff\u2019s death would help lay the ghost to rest, something Riley insisted was very important. They bound and gagged the Sheriff, took a few supplies and items from his home that wouldn\u2019t be missed, and hoped that the lack of any sign of struggle or robbery would create some confusion as to what had happened.<br /> <br /> Abram then led the group to Sioc\u2019s Cavern. Elsie stood outside to keep watch, and to mind Terah. Abram carried the bound Sheriff into the cavern, with Riley leading the way. With the route still fresh in their mind from earlier that night, Riley was able to navigate their way through the mine unerringly. They had no torches, but even without light they soon found their feet resting on the edge of the underground lake. Abram strode into the water and almost tripped over Sioc. He knelt down and made contact.<br /> <br /> Sioc seemed generous and willing to honour their proposed trade. He said he would ensure the ghost\u2019s dissolution in return for the Sheriff\u2019s life. Abram stepped away from the communion, double-checked with Riley that the terms were acceptable, and then went to undo the Sheriff\u2019s bonds. They wanted it to look like he had given his life to Sioc of his own free will.<br /> <br /> This gave the Sheriff the opportunity he\u2019d been looking for. He tried to struggle free, but Abram clamped his arms down around him. The two struggled in the cold waters of the cavern, the Sheriff trying to worm his way free, Abram trying to force him to his knees. Riley tried to look for an opening to help, but the Sheriff would duck or push them away or position Abram between the two of them with every try.<br /> <br /> Slowly, inexorably, Abram bore down on the human. He pinned one arm, then the other, pushing down until the Sheriff\u2019s knees gave way. Then, in one smooth movement, he seized the Sheriff bodily and hurled him into Sioc\u2019s twisted mass. There was screaming, thrashing, the sound of water splashing and vegetation crunching. And then everything went quiet.<br /> <br /> Abram spoke again with Sioc, who told them that their wish was granted. The ghost would have moved on. When Abram asked him to keep this meeting secret, however, Sioc said that his gardener would know regardless, for they are bound. Riley wanted to head back into town and see that the Mayor answer for his part in this, but Abram convinced them that they were out of time. They were going to have to flee Joseph\u2019s Cross.<br /> <br /> Leaving the cavern took a little longer than entering it, but it was still dark when they reached the entrance and met up with Elsie. The throng set off north, following the vague directions Riley had been given. They avoided the roads and the few intervening farms, and soon the arid but fertile lands around Joseph\u2019s Cross gave way to dust and devastation.<br /> <br /> The throng saw no signs of pursuit from Joseph's Cross. They walked north for two days, taking infrequent rests. The supplies they had gathered in Joseph's Cross meant they had no problems with food or water for Baby and Terah, let alone themselves. The wind never truly picked up, staying just strong enough to put a haze in the air and occasionally throw grit into the Prometheans' eyes.<br /> <br /> On the evening of the second day they spotted a farmstead ahead of them. After Joseph's Cross it looked decrepit and ruined, but there were still cows and a large number of pigs grazing in its fallow fields. The throng approached, noting a car with its wheels removed and its bonnet open sitting in the shadow of the house, and knocked on the door. It was answered by a wizened nut of a man, old and tanned and wrinkled. He tried to shoo them away and slam the door in their faces, but Elsie jammed her foot in the gap and the throng all but forced their way inside. The man's wife, similarly shrunken, watched without a word from the kitchen where she was washing dishes after what had evidently been an early evening meal.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans introduced themselves and asked if they could stay the night. The man, who reluctantly gave his name as Bertram, excused himself to discuss the matter with his wife. Riley burned Pyros to augment their senses and eavesdrop on the conversation, and distinctly heard Bertram mention the gun out the back. His wife urged him to wait. Riley relayed this to the other Prometheans in a soft whisper before Bertram returned.<br /> <br /> Riley and Abram opted to pretend that they needed to use the toilet, and Bertram showed them to the outhouse. He went back inside rather than watch over them, and they began to circle around the house to Terah and retrieve their weapons. Riley dispatched their spirit companion to check out the barn, and it came rushing back hissing something about a predator. Having seized up their weapons they head back inside to find Bertram pointing a shotgun at Elsie.<br /> <br /> Despite their weapons, Bertram held firm in the face of their attempts to get him to release his gun. He ordered them off his property. Riley mentioned that they know what is in the barn, and Bertram immediately became visibly scared. He turned the gun towards them and ordered them to go to the barn. He claims they have doomed themselves, and that he isn't responsible from this point forward.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans decided that, so long as they have their weapons, they aren't too scared by whatever might be waiting for them. They allowed Bertram to march them to the barn. Riley opened the barn door, and the stench of salt and iron, previously undetectable, washed over them. They stepped across the threshold.<br /> <br /> The barn was more of a slaughterhouse. Carcasses hung from hooks from the ceiling. The oldest, little more than skeletons with some tattered fur, were clearly dogs. The freshest bodies, still dripping blood, were cows. The ground was damp underfoot. There were drying stains on the walls. <br /> <br /> At the far end of the barn was a small, huddled figure in a stained dress, their features hidden by matted hair. It shivered at the sound of their footsteps. Curled around this figure was an enormous black mass. The mass stirred and rose to its feet and the Prometheans could see that it was a bloated black pig somehow grown to the size of a bear. Its head, tiny for its body mass and almost buried among the folds of fat, yawned open and idly clamped down on the shoulder of the huddled child. They could see small rivulets of blood seeping into the dress from where they stood. The pig's jaws worked slowly, then pulled away with a sucking sound. It ambled towards them, taking its time, but when it was about halfway across the barn it stopped and its little eyes narrowed down until they were almost slits.<br /> <br /> And then the pig spoke, its mouth moving in unnatural ways as it slurred out a handful of English words.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that you, Riley?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:26:31-07:00","id":1073452,"title":"","content":"Malik...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:50:48-07:00","id":1073461,"title":"","content":"Haha, we were joking that it'd be pretty funny if someone completed their pilgrimage and turned into a pig or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:52:43-07:00","id":1073463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1073461#post1073461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha, we were joking that it'd be pretty funny if someone completed their pilgrimage and turned into a pig or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Sublimatus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:55:24-07:00","id":1073466,"title":"","content":"And their was that Promethean Raven who became a normal raven when his pilgrimage ended. If some Promethean pulled the Demiurgic ritual with a \ud83d\udc37, you could have a Promethean who achieved a Porcine New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:56:34-07:00","id":1073468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1073463#post1073463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking Sublimatus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Malik himself was one? Interesting theory.<br /> <br /> We'll find out next time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:44:32-07:00","id":1075727,"title":"","content":"Chapter 7 \u2013 A Pig in Muck<br /> <br /> Riley wracked their brain as they stared at the Black Pig. They must have known it when they travelled with Malik, the two of them were always accompanied by a great host of spirits. Malik referred to them as his throng. They recalled that among those spirits had been a creature of indulgence and gluttony, the most likely culprit for the tableau before them. They were sure that they knew the creature, in spite of the fact that it had since Claimed a pig.<br /> <br /> The Black Pig seemed to have no interest in attacking them. This baffled Abram, as they watched Riley bend down to speak to the creature. That Riley would want to talk with the source of so much horror was disconcerting to him. Riley, meanwhile, found out that the spirit had left Malik when he told it that he was going to the north to seek out the Thing that dwells among the Dead Trees. The Bone Fields. The spirit had no idea what that Thing was, exactly, but it seemed to have an instinctive dread of the place. Riley got the impression that some other spirits had stayed with it, but that it had eaten them all in the weeks since.<br /> <br /> Abram began creeping closer to the girl as the conversation wound on. Unfortunately, Riley was having a hard time keeping the pig\u2019s sole attention and Abram was not naturally stealthy. The pig turned its head and openly watched his every move. Yet it showed no intention of being hostile, telling Riley that it wouldn't touch any of their friends. When Riley asked what the purpose of the girl was, the pig replied that it made sure the humans would keep it fed rather than it needing to hunt for food. It seemed to feel that its treatment was perfectly normal, given the nature of the universe. Humans did terrible things to livestock, but when the animals were stronger it was only right that humans experience life in the slaughterhouse.<br /> <br /> Abram\u2019s examination of the girl found that she was covered in filth, gore, and tears. Her dress was irreparably stained. Her hair was matted. Her skin was covered in open wounds, many of them infected. Two fingers from her right hand had been chewed off, the rotten stumps ending just before the knuckle in unsealed wounds. Her skin was cold and clammy, and Abram knew she needed medical attention immediately. She was largely unresponsive to Abram\u2019s attentions and attempts to get her to talk. Her gaze remained distant, staring into space.<br /> <br /> Abram reported this to Riley, and the two of them talked this over with the Black Pig. The spirit seemed confused by the situation. It seemed to think that eating was the only thing a being had to do to stay well, and it protested that it had been feeding the girl. It then demonstrated that fact by padding over, taking a great bite out of one of the cow carcasses, and then approaching the girl and prodding her with one trotter until she held out her hands. It then deposited the offal and flesh into her hands. She obediently raised her meal to her mouth and began to chew.<br /> <br /> Struggling to keep control of his temper, Abram told the pig she needed something else. He got her to stop eating, took off his jacket and shirt, and gave the latter to her. Doing so exposed his damaged chest, the vast swathes of missing skin and flesh, and the canary lodged inside his body. Riley and Elsie hadn't seen this sight before, and the sight shocked them. Abram was a little taken aback, he'd assumed such bodily trauma was normal for Prometheans, and for a few moments it seemed like the rest of the throng was on the verge of stripping naked to prove him wrong.<br /> <br /> Abram didn't want to be distracted from helping the girl, however. Riley persuaded the pig to let them get help, and it graciously told them that it considered the throng its guests, not prisoners. Abram went outside and found Bertram on guard. He told the man that his granddaughter would die unless he brought medical equipment and the contents of Abram\u2019s pillowcase, which was tied to Terah. The pillowcase was where Abram had stored most of the supplies stolen from the sheriff in Joseph's Cross. Bertram was stunned, but he was all too willing to believe in anything that might help his granddaughter. He ran off, and soon he and his wife were back with supplies. He pleaded with Abram not to let Hope die, which Abram entirely misinterpreted as some sort of metaphor.<br /> <br /> Back inside, Abram attempted to treat Hope\u2019s wounds. She flew into a rage though when he tried to tough her fingers and lashed out, clawing at his face. Riley and Abram were able to hold her down and Elsie began to croon soft, meaningless things to soothe her until she held still. Releasing her slowly, Abram began to wash her wounds. The finger stumps would need to be amputated, but he still lacked a knife or cleaver and felt it would be best to wait.<br /> <br /> The pig sat by her side through all this, visibly confused. Riley attempted to write a message while it was distracted, telling Abram that they needed to kill the pig, only to find out that Abram was illiterate. Abram, once he had finished and cleaned his hands, responded by drawing an incredible picture of Riley in the muck. He seemed to think that Riley was attempting to communicate via picture. As all attempts at silent communication failed over the next half an hour, they had to wait until the pig fell asleep to concoct a plan. Riley felt the pig would need to be killed, or at least severed from its corporeal existence. Elsie would grab Hope and flee the barn, the two of them would try to end the creature.<br /> <br /> They slept in shifts. Riley had nightmares of circling crows, a flock so large they filled the air like a storm. They woke to the sun rising, Pyros burning again in their veins. Abram opened the door to the barn and the sunlight spilled in, causing the pig to stir. Riley had prepared their shotgun, and they rushed to fire off a shot. They were too nervous, however, and the shot went wide.<br /> <br /> The next few seconds were a frenzy of movement. Elsie grabbed Hope and ran for the door. Abram charged the pig and drove his pickaxe into its flank. The pig screamed, the noise almost unbearable. It struggled to its feet and its flesh began to ripple. Abram struck it again, carving another bloody furrow down its side, but now he could see the wound begin to suck close.<br /> <br /> Then Riley fired their second shot, the blast opening an immense hole in the pig's flank. Gasping, bleeding, the creature looked at them and screamed at the betrayal. As Riley backed up, yelling that they couldn't let it hurt a family. The pig's head swung between Riley and Abram, and they could see its tears.<br /> <br /> &quot;We were a family!&quot; it bellowed at Riley. Then it charged. <br /> <br /> Riley burned their Pyros to summon an armoured skin. The pig's teeth skittered across their body, unable to find solid purchase. There was another meaty impact as Abram hooked one of the pig's legs, and in its moment of distraction Riley jammed the shotgun beneath the pig's head and pulled the trigger. With a tremor that shook the ground beneath their feet, it collapsed.<br /> <br /> Abram wasn't finished. He had seen the way the pig's flesh regenerated from even the most horrendous wounds. He walked up and in two mighty blows severed its head from its body, drenching Riley in gore in the process. The sensation of Vitriol boiling into being in his chest, a validation of his physical prowess, removed him from the horror of his surroundings for one perfect moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T04:28:11-07:00","id":1075833,"title":"","content":"Ah. So it wasnt a horribly mutated Malik. Thank The Principle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T03:18:49-07:00","id":1083903,"title":"","content":"Chapter 8 \u2013 The Bone Fields<br /> <br /> OOC Note: We had no session last week, one player was out of town and another busy with coursework. We were missing Elsie's player this week sadly.<br /> <br /> Abram strode from the barn into the light of the new day, shirtless and slick with pig blood. The humans were busy fussing over their granddaughter but they stopped for a moment, stunned and horrified at the sight of him. He caught Elsie\u2019s eye who, clearly surmising that the pig was dealt with and that she wasn\u2019t needed to drag Hope around anymore, happily wandered off to play with Baby.<br /> <br /> Bertram approached him and stammered out a few questions, but Abram silenced him by declaring that the pig was dead. He then went into the homestead, tracking blood and muck across the floor, until he found a Bible. The previous night\u2019s conversation had given him some ideas he wanted to test. He flipped the book open and stared at it, turning through the pages, staining them with his fingerprints. Then he went outside, collected his pillowcase, and made for the water pump to wash away the night\u2019s toils.<br /> <br /> He and Riley had made plans to leave soon, once Riley was sure that the spirit hadn\u2019t abandoned its Claimed body and taken up residence nearby, and after Riley had been given a chance to heal from their injuries. Abram busied himself collecting supplies. He asked Bertram what the family was willing to offer, and ended up with some shotgun shells and the Bible.<br /> <br /> Riley, meanwhile, didn\u2019t feel that they could face the family after what had happened. They lurked in the barn, smoking the more unspoilt sections of the carcasses in the barn to make rations for the Prometheans. When Abram returned, they asked him to ask the humans what they intended to do with the barn. When Abram asked, Bertram\u2019s reply was a simple, \u201cBurn it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Around midday of the following day Bertram came to Abram and told him that he needed to take his family into town. Hope needed a doctor\u2019s care, since gangrene appeared to be setting in on her wounds. He had disassembled his car on the pig\u2019s orders to make it more difficult for his family to flee, but he still had the pieces. By the end of the day he had reassembled it. He told the Prometheans that they were welcome to anything they wanted from the house, and then he was gone.<br /> <br /> That night, as the others slept, Abram painted his life\u2019s story on the barn\u2019s walls.<br /> <br /> One more day passed. Riley was still recovering from their injuries sustained from dealing with Sioc, and the encounter with the pig hadn\u2019t helped. Now though, they felt well enough to leave. They set fire to the barn, made sure it spread, until the entire building was consumed by the inferno. Then the throng moved on, a pillar of smoke at their backs.<br /> <br /> It was slow going from that point forward. The land became like a desert, their feet sank into the dust with every step. For two days they struggled through the wasteland, until they reached the edge of the region marked on Riley\u2019s map as \u201cthe Bone Fields\u201d.<br /> <br /> There was a permanent haze in the air, making visibility poor enough that seeing beyond fifty feet away became difficult. But they could see the trees. The lone trunks dotted the landscape, here and there, long dead and bleached white.<br /> <br /> In spite of everything, they found the empty camp quickly. It lay in the lee of a toppled tree trunk, but Riley found it unerringly. They immediately sensed the presence of an Athanor as they drew closer, the beacon of Azoth guiding them to a revolver among the belongings scattered around the campsite. Riley recognised it as a Firestorm Athanor. They checked the gun\u2019s chambers. It had been fired twice.<br /> <br /> Among the saddlebags spilling their contents into the dust they found strange little odds and ends. Doll\u2019s heads, slivers of bone, a bag of teeth, small totems and other items that Riley recognised. These were Malik\u2019s belongings. There was no sign of the elder Promethean however, and when Riley checked Twilight they saw no sign of the spirit menagerie that accompanied their maker.<br /> <br /> They kept heading north. They found a copse of dead trees, where wind chimes hung from the branches. There was a small hillock just beyond. As they drew closer they paused to examine the wind chimes, and found them to be a mixture of human and animal bones. And then they sensed the stomach roiling presence of flux, and the hillock began to move.<br /> <br /> It was a dormant Pandoran, but far larger than the Azothic Memory led them to expect. As it stirred free of its dormancy and the dust fell from its corpulent mass they saw hardened chitin, cracked in places and oozing a clear fluid. The armour gave way to soft flesh around its belly, where a thick umbilical cord trailed down and into the dust. Its head was dominated by immense jaws, ringed with insect-like mandibles bristling with teeth. Drool dripped from its mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, children, how sweet you smell,\u201d it gasped out. It moved faster than they expected, barrelling into Abram and bowling him over. He roared as it buried its face in his guts, ripping enormous chunks away in a feeding frenzy. Then, mouth full, it curled in on itself and began to chew furiously.<br /> <br /> Riley raced past, keeping control of Terah in spite of the horse\u2019s fear. They reached down and grasped Abram\u2019s hand, hauling him from the dust and onto the back of the horse behind them. Else was already fleeing, and they took off in her direction. As they rode the wind began to build, dust rising with it. They heard a bellow behind them, and then a sound like the crack of a great whip. A tree to their left shattered, and Riley glimpsed the Pandoran\u2019s umbilical cord being hauled back out of sight. Already it was becoming impossible to see, dust whirling around them faster and faster. They were in the centre of a Black Blizzard, springing up out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Keeping close together, desperate not to lose each other in the storm, the throng fled into the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:12:25-07:00","id":1087126,"title":"","content":"Chapter 9 \u2013 Firestorm<br /> <br /> The throng raced through the dust, stumbling almost blind in search of a way to escape their pursuer. They could hear the Pandoran on their trail, its heavy breathing echoing over even the howling winds of the Black Blizzard. They never laid sight on it, but they never lost the sound. The desperate, scrambling minutes dragged on, pushing through the storm, dust filling their eyes and noses and mouths. A massive shape loomed out of the storm and they shied away instinctively before they realised that it was a just another dead tree. They paused there and realised they could no longer hear the breathing. Riley dropped from Terah\u2019s saddle, giving the exhausted horse a reprieve from carrying the weight of two Prometheans, and checked on Abram. The Tammuz was clutching his wound, but he didn\u2019t appear to be in any immediate danger.<br /> <br /> Then the dust erupted around them, and the beast was on top of them. Terah screamed. Elsie reacted the fasted. She reached up and thrust Baby into Abram\u2019s arms. Riley struck Terah, and the horse took off carrying Abram away. The beast snarled, but it made no move to chase the horse. The two cornered Prometheans were the more tempting prey.<br /> <br /> It moved slowly now, confident that it had won. Its head drifted between Elsie and Riley. This close, they could make out the traces of humanity they had not had time to notice when it first attacked. Despite its huge size and insect-like mandibles, its head followed the curvature of a human skull. They could see cheekbones and traces of other features, but they fixated on the eyes. It had two human eyes, far too small for its head, squinting at them.<br /> <br /> The Pandoran sniffed, looked at Riley closely, and growled out, \u201cAre you ill, little one? Ill or wounded? Come to Typhoeus. He will make it better.\u201d<br /> <br /> Riley shivered. They made no move forward.<br /> <br /> This seemed to frustrate Typhoeus. His mandibles clicked. A few tense seconds passed, and then, \u201cI apologise for before. I did not mean to hurt any of you. But I was burned dry. I could not control myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Riley glared up at him. \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d<br /> <br /> Typhoeus\u2019s head withdrew. He fixed his gaze on Elsie instead, and declared that he wanted a child. Not some budding from his own flesh, but a child of his own blood. Kin to himself, Prometheans like them. He asked them to stay, to be his children, for him to care for and stroke and pet.<br /> <br /> Elsie stepped forward. The movement took Riley by surprise, they were too late to grab her and hold her back. She walked right up to Typhoeus and reached out a hand to stroke the chitin of his closest limb. The massive Pandoran leaned in to the gesture, curling its body around her to shield her from the wind and dust of the blizzard. In that small bubble Elsie smiled her most brilliant smile and told Typhoeus exactly what he wanted to hear. She admired his strength, his raw power, his dominion over this land. His physical form was something she thought should be admired. The beast made a sound in its throat that could almost have been a ghastly purr. Then, collecting itself, it asked her if she would stay with him.<br /> <br /> He never got an answer. Riley had pulled the revolver they had found in Malik\u2019s camp from their jacket, and aimed it into the air. They pulled the trigger. The world exploded in fire and lightning.<br /> <br /> Amidst Typhoeus\u2019s screams, the roar of the storm, the roll of thunder, the rage of the Firestorm, Riley grabbed Elsie and dragged her away from the thrashing Pandoran. They ran as fast as they could, their clothes beginning to smoulder. The bone-dry trees of the Bone Fields had ignited. They could see them through the storm, pillars of fire blazing like beacons. The wind whipped flame into a chaotic maelstrom of flying streams and eddies.<br /> <br /> Typhoeus rose behind them, fire streaming across his armoured body. His head pulled back, his maw yawned open, and a stream of bile jetted out at Riley. They ducked, the corrosive liquid raining droplets on them, but they were unharmed. Then the fire roared up in front of them, a wall of flame without mercy. Riley stared at it, looked at Elsie, and back at Typhoeus. With no other choice, the Prometheans stepped through it together.<br /> <br /> They emerged out the other side. Riley was screaming and clutching their left arm, the flames burning right to the bone. Their Pyros-infused flesh was burning no less fiercely than the dead trees all around them. To their right, Elsie was staring straight ahead, her face blank. Her hair and neck burned, but she paid it little mind, as though something had snapped inside. She ran forward, continuing to flee, mechanically and without a glance at Riley. Gritting their teeth, Riley rushed to catch up.<br /> <br /> Typhoeus was slowed by the same wall of fire. In the chaos and confusion they soon lost sight of him. Lightning strikes struck all around them in waves, one bolt lancing straight into Riley\u2019s chest. Their fingers and toes curled as the energies coursed through them, reinvigorating them, healing the remains of their wounds from Sioc. It gave them enough energy to attempt one last attempt to evade their pursuer. Riley poured their remaining Pyros into igniting an alchemical transmutation within their body. They grew larger, dropping to four legs. In moments they had mimicked Terah\u2019s form. Elsie clambered on and Riley called on newfound strength.<br /> <br /> The firestorm burned out after only a few seconds, but Typhoeus was not so easily shaken. They rode through the blizzard for what felt like hours, the massive Pandoran keeping pace with Riley at times, at others lagging behind, but always on their trail. At last Riley broke free from the storm, the dust clearing from the air so suddenly it was as if a knife had been used to mark the storm\u2019s edge. Up ahead they could see a line of silver running straight across the horizon. A railway line.<br /> <br /> They raced the storm. It roiled and curled behind them, pursuing them, Typhoeus hidden somewhere within it. A train came into view, coming from the north. Riley could see Abram and Terah well ahead of them, angling towards the train as well. As they drew level, a door in the side of one of the train\u2019s containers was hauled back. Terah seemed to require no urging, leaping inside.<br /> <br /> Riley could almost feel Typhoeus\u2019s breath on their neck. They lengthened their stride for one final burst. They followed in Terah\u2019s footsteps, aiming for the same carriage hauled by the long freight train. The door was still open. As they drew closer, they could see a figure standing in the opening. They recognised him. A weathered man, his age indeterminate, they had last seen on the night Malik left them. The man that had driven them apart.<br /> <br /> Elsie, for her part, also recognised the man. He had sold her a radio a few weeks ago, something she still carried with her. He had said his name was John Shepherd. They were close enough to touch. She stood up, keeping her balance on the back of a galloping horse with astonishing grace, and held out a hand. Shepherd took it, and she stepped daintily from the horse into the darkness of the carriage. She had to step quickly to one side, as a few seconds later Riley leapt aboard.<br /> <br /> The carriage door was hauled shut. The storm hit. The interior of the carriage went completely dark.<br /> <br /> Elsie found her way to Baby and nursed him as she listened to the Black Blizzard rage. Only the leading edge of the storm caught them before they left it behind, and it could not reach them inside. She settled down, listening as the others moved around. She called out to Shepherd. He spoke from behind her, and the two sat in the dark and talked. She prompted him to hold Baby, which he appeared to find intensely uncomfortable, and then asked him if he knew what had chased them. He said he did. It was a monster born in the mines to the west by a ritual gone awry. Its birthplace had been filled with Prometheans, and it had gorged, grown strong, and made its way to the Dust Bowl in search of food.<br /> <br /> When light began to return to the carriage, John Shepherd was gone. Riley had holed up in a corner, as far from where Elsie and Shepherd had been sitting as possible. There were several other occupants in the carriage, hobos from the north. They had pushed the crates in the half-empty carriage up against the walls and made a nice little camp for themselves. Elsie chatted with a man who introduced himself as Damien Sharp, who became very friendly when she mentioned that she was friends with John Shepherd. \u201cAny friend of John\u2019s is a friend of ours,\u201d he told her.<br /> <br /> They found that the train was heading to Sour Springs. The hobos hoped to find work there or in Wakesfield, further down the line. Riley drifted off to sleep, but Elsie wasn\u2019t able to relax in the rattling, clanking carriage. When they arrived at Sour Springs the hobos disembarked quickly, before they could be found, and split up once they hit the streets. The throng made its way through Sour Springs, finding it a quiet town with many empty, abandoned buildings. They found a shop not too far from the centre of town that was visibly empty, and chose it as a place to stay while they were in town.<br /> <br /> The empty shelves and a pile of blankets in one corner of the room showed that this place had been used by squatters before, but not recently to judge by the dust. Here, at last, Elsie was able to get some sleep. Riley, a small measure of Pyros returned by the recent sunrise, peered into Twilight after noticing that their spirit companion was fixated on something in the corner of the room. They looked and found a small, grub-like creature about the size of a cat. It stirred under their gaze and looked up at them with the face of a child but weathered and lined like an old man\u2019s. The dirt caking its face was parted by tear trails running down its cheeks.<br /> <br /> The creature didn\u2019t appear to understand English. It certainly made no attempt to reply to Riley\u2019s words. Their spirit companion didn\u2019t seem threatened by the creature, just alert. In the end they decided to wait out the day. They were all injured, Riley had no interest in speaking to any human and wanted time to mull over the appearance of John Shepherd, and it seemed safest to stay hidden just for now. They drifted off to sleep later that night, one by one.<br /> <br /> Riley opened their eyes. They were lying where they had been when they fell asleep. It felt like only moments had passed, but they didn\u2019t feel tired anymore. They looked around the room and could see Abram and Elsie there, but something had certainly changed. The windows of the store were now shattered, but there was no glass on the floor. Riley stepped outside.<br /> <br /> It could almost be Sour Springs, if they turned their head to the side and squinted. The shattered windows and broken doors of the houses gave them the look of gruesome, damaged faces. Some of the buildings were a lot larger than they had been in daylight, and Riley realised that it was as if the buildings were moving in the corner of their eye, crawling on one another, feeding. Above it all loomed the Town Hall Clocktower. It had been a squat, simple structure in the daylight. Now it was this immense gothic monolith, adorned in spires and gargoyles. Riley rushed back inside to find the store\u2019s shelves were now full, each shelf stocking a different human bone.<br /> <br /> They knew they were dreaming but, somehow, they also knew with unerring certainty that Elsie and Abram were in this dream with them. There was no sign of Baby, Terah, or Riley\u2019s spirit companion. They went outside, together, and looked up at the tower looming over them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:24:24-07:00","id":1089622,"title":"","content":"Chapter 10 \u2013 The Nightmare of Sour Springs<br /> <br /> Abram called out, his voice echoing through the empty streets. Riley hushed him hurriedly, but it was too late. They heard howls in response, seeming to come from every direction at once. The three Prometheans set off towards the tower at once, jogging down the middle of the road, when they heard a low voice hiss at them from a broken doorway. They saw a young woman holding an axe in front of her, beckoning them urgently.<br /> <br /> Up close the woman had coarse, blunt features and was dressed in little more than rags. The house they were standing in was in ruins, every piece of furniture had been smashed to pieces. Once they were all inside, she asked them what the hell they were doing. It came out that it was their first night in Sour Springs. The woman introduced herself as Marcy. In the background Elsie busied herself collecting scraps of cloth and cushion fragments from among the debris. Then they heard the footsteps.<br /> <br /> They all took cover at Marcy\u2019s urging. The beast\u2019s smell came first, a thick musk and the stench of wet fur. It was a large, heavyset creature, bigger than Abram. Its furred body was like that of an enormous ape, though its head put them more in mind of a toad. Its broad mouth hung open as it walked, giving Riley, lurking in the doorway, a view of its wide, red gullet ringed with row after row of teeth.<br /> <br /> Once it had passed the throng turned to Marcy and demanded to know about the creature. They found out that it and two others like it haunted the dream, hunting the people of Sour Springs night after night. Dying in the dream didn\u2019t kill you, but you had to endure a very lifelike death and you always woke sore and feeling bruised from the experience. That description sounded like a challenge to Abram. He had refused to shift from his Soldier Role since completing it, and felt like his failure to stand up to Typhoeus needed to be rectified. He offered to help Marcy with the town\u2019s problem, and asked if anyone had tried to kill the beasts. She told him that the prisoners and guards from the town lock-up formed a mob each night and tried to bring the beast down. Sometimes they even succeeded, but most nights they just died in droves. It didn\u2019t seem to be achieving anything.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans had fixated on the immense clocktower that the town hall had become. With the coast clear, they left Marcy in her hiding spot and made their way towards it. Abram collected some of the black bile from his still-oozing wounds and used it to start painting on the wall of the clocktower, once they found there was no visible entrance. Then they took up hiding spots in the nearby buildings and waited for a beast to show itself.<br /> <br /> The creature that appeared was closer to a humanoid wolf. Its crocodilian muzzle was grey with age, and it moved with a grace the thunderous creature from before had been lacking. It reached Abram\u2019s artwork and sniffed, clearly picking up his scent. Then Riley shot it in the back. It howled, and the others rushed from hiding. Abram struck it with his pickaxe, sinking it deep. Elsie threw herself onto the beast, trying to find its neck through the fur. The two writhed together, the swirling mass of fur and flesh making it impossible for Riley to get a clear bead on the beast for a second shot. They charged instead and threw themselves into the scrum.<br /> <br /> It was to no avail. The creature\u2019s fur began to crackle with energy, rising into a shimmering corona of Pyros-infused lightning. The blast swept out from it, striking Abram and sending him convulsing to the ground, the light dying from his eyes. It twisted and seized Elsie\u2019s arm in its jaws, clamping down and tearing it free from her body. As she crumpled it flung Riley from its back, pinning them to the ground. The last thing Riley saw was its jaws closing in.<br /> <br /> They woke in the early hours of the morning, aching and sore. After some discussion they decided further heroics would need to wait until their wounds had healed. Instead they went to visit the town hall in daylight. The plain, wooden building with its short clocktower sported no sign of the painting Abram had made in the dream, to his disappointment. Sadly, they were unable to get past the clerk in the lobby. He refused to let them in without an appointment, and refused to let them make an appointment. The best they were able to get was a set of directions to the office. They passed a morbidly obese man struggling up the stairs as they left, but paid him no mind.<br /> <br /> Days passed, as they waited for the burns they had suffered in the Firestorm to healed. They stayed inside their abandoned building in their waking hours and in their sleep. Every night the dream appeared to reset, and they rebuilt hasty fortifications to keep the monsters out night after night. During daylight Riley would make a show of reading the Bible, hoping to provoke Abram into asking to learn. Abram, for his part, got a glimmer of Riley\u2019s intent through their shared brand. He relented, and asked for some lessons.<br /> <br /> That night, when their eyes opened into the nightmare of Sour Springs, they felt ready. They stepped out into the street together, eager for another chance at the beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T00:15:04-07:00","id":1102722,"title":"","content":"when will this come back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:13:13-07:00","id":1102747,"title":"","content":"Apparently, the players have been quite busy with real life things recently. I know Riley's player has had a fair bit of Uni work to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:28:31-07:00","id":1102775,"title":"","content":"Well thats sad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T15:34:28-07:00","id":1103307,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the long delay. I've been in and out of the city, then the university students among us got hammered by the end of semester, but it's calmed down now and we had our first session in over a month on Sunday. Was planning on working on the write-up today, so we'll see how that goes. It was a short session as we tried to get our collective heads back into the game.<br /> <br /> We should be back to regular weekly games now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T20:25:01-07:00","id":1103369,"title":"","content":"Chapter 11 - Everything is fine<br /> <br /> Riley stood in the shadows of a doorway across the street from their shelter in Sour Springs. They were in the nightmare, taking their first steps outside in several weeks. Elsie was standing on the street corner, idly looking at the sky.<br /> <br /> A tile smashed onto the street. The two Prometheans turned, and looked up. The distorted silhouette of the closest building became a roaring, leaping blur of teeth and fur. Elsie stepped neatly out of the way just before it reached her and the large, greying wolf-like beast slammed into the pavement, cracking it with the force of its impact.<br /> <br /> They had a brief moment where they recognised the beast as the same creature they had fought before, at the base of the tower. It was the older of the two beasts they had seen, lean with a greying muzzle. It turned towards Elsie, rising to shoulder height even on all fours. She stretched out a hand as if to stroke its head. The beast lunged straight at the proffered limb, tearing it away, before it pinned her to the ground and crushed her skull between its teeth.<br /> <br /> Riley was running before the beast's jaws snapped shut. They burst into the building and raced through the ruined interior, making for the back door. They slammed into it, but the door appeared to be jammed. Then, behind them, they heard the terrible sound of wood snapping and breaking as the beast forced its way through the wall. The house began to come apart. Riley pressed their back against the wall, just out of reach of the beast's flailing arms, and fired two shots into the creature's chest. The bullets made a strange sound as they struck home, and for a moment they could glimpse something like an armoured shell beneath the fur.<br /> <br /> Then a second massive, corpulent arm reached in through the ruin of the house's facade. It pulled away more of the roof and wall, and the bloated beast Riley had seen when they hid with Marcy on their first night in the nightmare pulled itself into view. Its arms reached for them, seized Riley before they could get out of the way, and pulled them into a rib-snapping embrace. This seemed to anger the first, older beast. It lashed out, tearing chunks from the larger beast's face. Riley's face was spattered with a clear, viscous liquid that flew from the wound. They struggled, to no success, unable to get free. They felt their hair rise to stand on end and smelt the tell-tale trace of ozone as the older beast's fur began to crackle with lightning. The blast swept outward, and Riley was knocked free to die, shuddering, on the floor.<br /> <br /> Elsie and Riley woke not long after, feeling sore and bruised. The injuries faded quickly, but it was a couple of hours before dawn started to creep in through the window and either of them felt like moving again. In the meantime they talked over their plans. Riley was resolved to staying in Sour Springs for some time, at least until they could pick up Malik's trail once again. In the meantime they wanted to help the people here. Dealing with the pig spirit had inspired them, they wanted to create a service for the people of Sour Springs where people could come to them for help with supernatural problems. Elsie offered to help by gathering together some supplies to make posters. She tore strips of wallpaper from the walls to serve as paper, but no one in the group had anything to write with. So she set off to get a pen.<br /> <br /> She returned about an hour later with the pen.<br /> <br /> Nothing bad happened.<br /> <br /> Everything is fine.<br /> <br /> Honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T20:29:39-07:00","id":1103372,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, part of the reason that write-up is so short is because it was a pretty short session. Abram's player couldn't make it and Elsie's player was late so we really only played for an hour and a half.<br /> <br /> The other reason it's so short is because Elsie- *muffled screaming*<br /> <br /> Damn that imagery is going to stay with me for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T21:27:03-07:00","id":1105279,"title":"","content":"Chapter 12 - Meanwhile...<br /> <br /> For once, Elsie had not taken Baby with her when she left the building. She had just left her wrapped up in the middle of the floor of their little hovel. Abram and Riley were engaged in the middle of a writing lesson when they heard her start to cry. Calling on some long unused instincts of his human body, Abram was able to calm the child while Riley hauled out any vegetables they had that weren't too rotten and set about boiling and mashing them.<br /> <br /> Together, they managed to feed Baby. Riley started asking Abram probing questions about how babies were made, and somehow the conversation ended up on prostitution. Riley ended up forcing an Elpis Vision, trying to divine if their future held any of these fascinating subjects. The cavalcade of vivid images did reveal to them an upcoming milestone that would require an extended period of time spent in close company with humans. The process infused the surrounding air with their humour, however, and the throng felt a Wasteland fester into being.<br /> <br /> Abram kept Baby with them for the next few hours, until Elsie returned. She was at once overjoyed to see Abram taking an interest in her child, and struggled to keep her jealousy at the attention from boiling over. She took Baby back, soothed her when she cried, and happily turned over the pen to Riley. When Riley tried to ask her how she'd gotten one, since she hadn't taken any money with her, she dodged the question. Poorly. She retreated with Baby to a corner of the room as the skeptical Riley noted that one of her shoes was damp. Between them, Riley and Abram agreed that Elsie must have certainly stolen the pen.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the throng put their suspicions aside and they all began to work on advertising posters. Elsie stripped wallpaper from the walls, Abram decorated them, and Riley wrote down details. Between the three of them they soon had a small pile of flyers and posters. The posters promised to help anyone who asked for help with their nightmares, and gave directions on how to contact the throng.<br /> <br /> It was starting to grow late again, and Abram and Riley had been discussing the Pyros-linked nature of the monsters in the dream. They figured that since fire worked particularly well on their own flesh, it may be similarly effective against the beasts. Since it seemed that they needed to have items in the real world to carry them over to the dream world, they decided to get their hands on some alcohol so they could make some flammable projectiles for the night ahead.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this proved more difficult than expected. A town the size of Sour Springs should surely have had a speakeasy or similar, but Abram was unable to persuade anyone to tell him where he could find it. They tried the General Store, but found it cordoned off and surrounded by a small crowd of horrified and distressed looking people. Rather than inquire they headed back to their lodgings, when they spotted the filthy-looking barbershop across the street. Aftershave could work in a pinch, Abram figured.<br /> <br /> The grimy shop turned out to be even worse on the inside. The door had been propped open, as if to invite in customers, but in doing so had allowed dust to blow in from the street. Dust, water, and hair had combined to make a thick sludge that pooled in the corners of the room, beneath the counter, and in any other moderately hard to reach spots. The barber, a thin, middle-aged man wearing stained clothes and smelling strongly of old sweat, got slowly to his feet and eyed Riley.<br /> <br /> &quot;It'll be extra for that one,&quot; he said, his voice low and hoarse.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans exchanged a look, not sure if he was referring to Riley's race or their long, thick hair. Abram carefully explained that they had come to buy some aftershave. The barber was quiet for far too long, before finally agreeing to go and get some for them. He shuffled off, returned with three bottles, and demanded a price far beyond that which Abram was willing to pay, certainly far more than the aftershave was worth. A warning hand from Riley was the only thing that stopped the scene from escalating to violence. Instead, Abram merely threatened the barber, grabbed the aftershave, and left behind a fraction of the asking price. For the barber's part he didn't put up a fight, merely shrinking away from the Prometheans and hiding his face.<br /> <br /> That night, as they dreamed, the Prometheans felt that they were at last prepared to take on the beasts. Abram was still feeling vindictive, so he made his way across to the dream-version of the barbershop and started to lay about with his pickaxe. He smashed open the rear wall of the store, where glistening scalps lay in place of hair, and stepped out into a new street where he could hear the sounds of fighting. The throng raced towards the noise and walked straight into the midst of a slaughter. Men, some manacled and clad in prisoner uniforms, others wearing the outfits of local deputies, were fighting a beast none of them had seen before. It was smaller than the other two, with paler fur. It was cornered against the wall of one building, but it was still lashing out with its claws at any man who got too close. The street was littered with dismembered bodies.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans wasted no time gawping. Abram hurled the first of their makeshift explosives at the beast, setting its fur ablaze. As it howled in pain, Riley hurled the second... but their aim went wide and flames quickly spread among the human mob. In the chaos Elsie quickly climbed up the side of a nearby building and hurled herself onto the beast's back, but she was unable to get a purchase and was thrown into a wall.<br /> <br /> The beast's jaws opened wide and a thick, grey fog rolled out. As it swept across the humans their faces fell and they cast their weapons away, throwing themselves to their knee. Riley breathed in the fog and felt the hopelessness of their situation. The beast was growing larger, visibly enraged but unharmed from their attacks. They knew this fight would never work. The flames roared over them as they stood there, unmoving, giving up all hope.<br /> <br /> Abram and Elsie were made of sterner stuff. The fire was roaring out of control, but they charged through the fire into the beast's open arms. The beast tore open Abram's chest, moments before he brought his pickaxe down on its head. Its skull split open and it collapsed, even as the fire consumed Abram's tendons and muscles. His limbs gave way and he collapsed to the street.<br /> <br /> Elsie alone saw the change that spread across the deputies as their quarry died. They threw their heads back, howled and picked up their weapons once more. She followed them as they charged through the streets, a savage pack looking for their next prey. Then they stumbled out onto the main street and found the elder beast waiting for them. Lightning crackled across its skin, and Elsie's last sight before she too succumbed was of the electricity dancing from man to man, downing each in turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 06-26-2017, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T22:21:41-07:00","id":1107901,"title":"","content":"Chapter 13 - The cracks are showing<br /> <br /> The characters woke from their disturbed, confused nightmares in the early hours of the morning. They spoke among themselves and resolved to locate the local speakeasy or equivalent gathering spot and try to find someone interested in hiring them on as supernatural investigators. Then they had to pass a few hours until the sun had risen. Abram whittled a ball from a lump of wood and played a simplistic game of catch with Riley, but the whole time he clearly had something on his mind. Tensions between him and Elsie over the disregard with which she treated Baby boiled over into a full-blown row. Elsie was more than happy to yell insults and recriminations back at Abram, though her attacks left him rather confused. Her every response to his criticisms of her parenting styles was to attack his, or Riley's, appearance. Riley, wanting no part of the argument, ran out to be with Terah. Eventually, Abram too left, leaving Elsie alone with Baby.<br /> <br /> Crooning over the child, Elsie resolved to make sure that the growing bond between Baby and Abram went no further. She activated her Weaponise Transmutation to force Disquiet into Baby's system, knowing that the attraction her Disquiet inspired would keep Baby close.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Abram conducted an early search of the town and found some men who informed him circumspectly that the place to get a drink locally was Mike's Roadhouse. The throng gathered together, a little reluctantly, to check it out and advertise their new supernatural problem solving business.<br /> <br /> They waited until midday before heading over. They found the roadhouse to be clean and almost entirely empty. The desk was unmanned. They struck the bell, and it took several minutes before a big, greasy man came through the back door. He sized them up, identified Abram as the leader, snorted, ran a hand through his hair, and went in for a handshake. He introduced himself as Mike, and asked if they were after rooms. Abram quickly gathered from the comments Mike made that the roadhouse itself must have no, or almost no, clients.<br /> <br /> It took a little bit of persuading to allow three strangers inside, but Abram was able to convince Mike of his credibility. They ended up through the back door and into the basement. A simple speakeasy-style arrangement had been set up there, with the walls decorated by sepia pictures of Sour Springs. There were two men at a table in the corner, a half-finished drink showing that Mike had clearly been with them.<br /> <br /> Riley and Elsie set up in a corner while Abram talked to the men. He wanted to find out if any of the men were interested in help with their dreams, but Mike seemed to interpret the questions as Abram looking for mob work and turned him down. When Abram clarified, he was laughed off.<br /> <br /> Over the next few hours, as men finished their working shifts, the roadhouse began to fill. Elsie took the opportunity to leave Baby with Riley and to start flirting with Mike. She was quickly the centre of attention, much to Abram's disapproval. She found out that Mike had a car, which was going to be used for an 8 o'clock delivery, and he promised to take her for a drive afterwards.<br /> <br /> In the midst of this one of the local labourers came up to Riley's table. He didn't introduce himself, and halfheartedly made fun of the idea of supernatural investigators. Then, in a lower voice, he asked to meet them the next day somewhere more private to discuss the matter.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans had realised by this point that the men in the room, and they were practically all men, were drinking slowly but steadily. It was a room of men who were not eager to return to their homes, who all seemed intent on dragging the night out to the early hours. No one wanted to go to their beds.<br /> <br /> Abram, unable to tolerate Elsie flirting with half the occupants of the room, left Riley alone in the bar. Not long after that, Mike led Elsie from the room to see his car, leaving Riley alone with the baby. Elsie saw three men, two young, one much older and distinguished who was clearly supervising, unloading barrels from the back of the car. Once they were done they went inside. She got into the car with Mike and they drove off, passing Abram on the way out of town and kicking dust into his face. He hurried after, arriving on the edge of town, but by then he'd lost them. He did, however, see something that sent him sprinting back to town to find Riley.<br /> <br /> Mike pulled to a stop a short drive from Sour Springs. Elsie, by this point, was busy evaluating him as prospective suitor material, and was insistently trying to suss out his opinion on children. When he seemed to dislike the idea she asked, &quot;Well, what about <i>my</i> children?&quot; Mike seemed to take that as an invitation, and leaned in to kiss her.<br /> <br /> Riley and Abram (and Baby) were staring at the horizon. It was hard to make out in the darkness, now that the sun had set, but there was a dust cloud to the south-east, in the direction of Joseph's Cross. The storm wasn't moving, which was concerning enough in its own right. They remembered the beast Typhoeus from the Bone Fields, and the storm that had followed it. When it was clear that there was nothing they could do about it this night, they walked back into town. Riley could tell that something else was bothering Abram. They pried, gently, but Abram's responses weren't exactly clear. Something about Elsie. Together with their connection as a Branded Throng, however, it was enough for Riley to work out what the issue was. Abram was jealous of Elsie, jealous of the way she attracted men, and at a loss on how to reconcile that jealousy with his role in the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T03:16:19-07:00","id":1108677,"title":"","content":"Do they have any character sheets? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T05:56:38-07:00","id":1108721,"title":"","content":"They do, though the players keep a hold of them so I don't have them on hand. I know Abram has Strength 6, but I'd be hard pressed to recall any other details right now sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:17:48-07:00","id":1109769,"title":"","content":"She's making Baby attracted to her...that is so wrong, but I so called her Disquiet becoming a problem for the human kid. But doing that on purpose, to a child no less, that is so wrong on so many levels.<br /> <br /> *thumbs up* keep up the good, disturbing work, you magnificent bastards<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, is Abram jealous of how Elsie attracts men because he is gay, or just because he envies how relatively easy it is for her to deal with people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 06-30-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T06:57:15-07:00","id":1110144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1109769#post1109769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's making Baby attracted to her...that is so wrong, but I so called her Disquiet becoming a problem for the human kid. But doing that on purpose, to a child no less, that is so wrong on so many levels.<br /> <br /> *thumbs up* keep up the good, disturbing work, you magnificent bastards</div> </div> </div> </div>Elsie... Elsie worries me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1109769#post1109769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, is Abram jealous of how Elsie attracts men because he is gay, or just because he envies how relatively easy it is for her to deal with people?</div> </div> </div> </div>A little of column A, a little of column B, but the specific realisation Riley had was the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T21:26:56-07:00","id":1111547,"title":"","content":"Session 14 - We're in business!<br /> <br /> The Prometheans retired to their makeshift home for the night. When they entered the nightmare Riley, desperate for a calm night's sleep to recover some of their energy, chose to run and hide. Abram just nursed Baby, making no particular effort to hide himself, until the front of the building was torn away by the elder beast. Abram promptly dropped Baby, callously deciding that the child would be fine in the end no matter what injury it suffered in dreams, and raced to snatch up the carefully prepared molotovs. As the beast clawed at him he began to hurl the molotovs at the floor, burning down the building with himself and Baby inside. Riley, hidden in an alcove further down the street, watched in horror as the flames spread from building to building. Humans were forced out of hiding and into the street, where the elder beast and its rival, the bloated, fat toad-like monster, fell upon the helpless victims.<br /> <br /> Riley survived the night, waking in the morning as Elsie burst through the door in the early hours of the morning. She refused to tell anyone how her date with Mike had gone, and instead she and Abram quickly got into another argument over parenting. Riley left before it escalated too badly, taking Terah for an early morning ride. They noted that the dust cloud appeared to have shrunk from the night before, just a discoloured splotch on the horizon.<br /> <br /> When she got back, both Abram and Elsie appeared to have decided they had won their argument. They decided that they wanted more alcohol to prepare more weapons to fight the monsters, and sent Elsie out to procure some. She found the roadhouse unmanned and, rather than ring the bell, just proceeded straight down to the speakeasy. She knocked on the door and it was opened by the old man she'd seen supervising the unloading of Mike's car the night before. He smiled at her, opened the door to let her see it was him and Mike inside. The man introduced himself as Carlisle West, and asked what she'd come for.<br /> <br /> Elsie was tired, hadn't slept, and couldn't be bothered to dissemble and persuade the men to give her alcohol. She bluntly told the man that she wanted to burn some buildings down, then began to burn her Pyros on the Weaponse and Redirect Alembics to turn Carlisle into a furious, raving lunatic who launched himself at Mike. As the two men brawled in the background she scooped up a few bottles of liquor and walked out, burning the last of her Pyros for good measure to turn the speakeasy into a Wasteland.<br /> <br /> The throng then waited until midday to meet with their potential client out the front of the barbershop. Riley was eager to be there first, so made sure to be outside a full hour before the agreed upon time. Abram spent the time standing next to them, staring through the dirty window of the barbershop at the barber inside. He noted that the man spent the entire time just staring at his own shoes, not moving. Elsie rejoined them, and their client arrived. He introduced himself as Peter Jones, and he and Riley agreed upon terms. He was poor, saving money to move to California where he hoped to find work. Instead of paying them, he would try and find out what he could about the nightmare. He told them that it had only been happening for a few months, so they asked him to find out if anyone new had come to town around then. In return they would protect him each night in the nightmare.<br /> <br /> This completed the Hermit role for Riley. They decided to move on from Cuprum, instead joining Elsie as a Plumbum in the Pilgrim role. They were determined to get Abram a date.<br /> <br /> The throng spent their afternoon visiting the sheriff at the county lock-up, hoping to learn more about why the deputies and prisoners were teaming up to fight the beasts in the nightmare. The sheriff flatly refused to speak about the nightmare though, telling them (in a rather patronising fashion) that while their dreams might seem real, they couldn't hurt them. Riley's protests that the dreams were obviously unnatural fell on deaf, or unwilling, ears.<br /> <br /> Dejected, Riley and Abram decided to go for a simple walk about town. Riley still hoped to pick up the trail of Malik, but so far it appeared to have gone cold. Stretching and testing the limits of their new Refinement, they used the Plumb the Fathoms Alembic to find out if there were any still-living Prometheans who had passed through Sour Springs. The Azothic Memory's response was that there were two.<br /> <br /> Almost on cue, the two Prometheans paused as they both sensed the same thing. An Azothic Radiance, coming from somewhere close. They had just walked past the Green Plains Bank, a local bank showing signs that it had been targeted by thrown projectiles in recent days. Abram suggested that perhaps they might be sensing the presence of an Athanor in the Bank's vaults. Stricken with indecision, the two of them stared up at the Bank's scarred facade, not sure what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T21:19:26-07:00","id":1115779,"title":"","content":"Session 15 - The Clocktower<br /> <br /> Riley and Abram briefly looked over the Green Plains Bank. They found the interior to show signs, here and there, of the hard times striking the entire region, but no clues as to what might be triggering their sensitivity to the Azothic Radiance. Rather than speak to anyone, they chose instead to walk back out quickly. They had returned to their makeshift home by the time Elsie returned with her bottles of alcohol, which she proudly displayed to them.<br /> <br /> After some discussion, the group decided to focus on the leadership of Sour Springs. There was clearly something going on at the Town Hall, between its massively distorted appearance in the dream and the fact that they had been unable to get past the front desk and talk to the mayor. Abram suggested that they find out where the mayor lived and try to catch him away from the office, so they went for a walk around town looking for the nicest houses.<br /> <br /> Riley, for their part, spent this walk sizing up the men of the town trying to work out what Abram's &quot;type&quot; might be. They figured someone like Abram, tall, muscular, fairly good-looking, but sadly pickings in Sour Springs seemed to be slim. They were down by the railway, inspecting the exterior of a building best described as a small mansion, when Riley spotted a nice-looking young man walking towards it. He was dressed in a duster and hat that made him look like a cowboy out of a western. He made straight for the building they were looking for, and Riley persuaded the other two to stage a distraction.<br /> <br /> With the sound of Abram and Elsie laying into each other in a half-real, half-pretend row about parenting techniques providing cover, Riley was able to sneak up to the window. Inside they could see the young man, his back to them, talking with a corpulent fat man wearing the finest clothes Riley had ever seen. He was slumped back in his chair, coated in sweat, and the allure of his clothing was somewhat spoiled by the sweat stains on the collar.<br /> <br /> Riley wasn't able to hear anything, but they had some small talent at reading lips and were able to determine that the fat man was expressing his frustration to the young man, whose name was Mikael, that the mayor was unreachable. Mikael's replies were impossible to make out, but eventually the fat man shrugged and said that &quot;Gant&quot; would not be a problem.<br /> <br /> When Mikael left the house, Riley tailed them until they found him taking a seat in front of the town hall, staring up at it. Riley returned to gather the other two, and the throng resolved to just break in. They entered the town hall and confront the clerk. When he, once again, refused to let them in without an appointment, Abram and Elsie staged another row and Riley was able to slip past the clerk and through the door behind him.<br /> <br /> The corridor behind reception was a long, featureless wooden corridor that curved slightly to the right. Riley followed it until they reached a door at the other end, but realised before they opened it that it was the door they had just come through. They realised that they needed to back up, back the way they thought they had just walked, and open the door they found behind them.<br /> <br /> That door led through to a stone corridor, lit with flickering torches. Riley had an easy feeling that they were somehow standing on a physical edge of the dream. They stepped inside and started to explore, finding the stone maze of corridors beyond looped back in on itself in confusing, even impossible ways.<br /> <br /> When Riley hadn't returned within a quarter of an hour of departing, Abram got impatient. He threatened the clerk with violence, and he bolted. Elsie and Abram walked through into the corridors beyond. Through a fluke of luck more than anything they were able to find the entrance to the stone corridors, but after that they became separated and very, very lost.<br /> <br /> Riley, unaware that the others were trying to follow, had used their newfound Alembics from the Plumbum Transmutation to access the Azothic Memory and guide them onward. They found the base of a long staircase they hoped would lead up to the tower. They began to climb. The stairs went on for what felt like forever, leading them up for more than an hour. They reached a landing, at last. The sound of gears turning and grinding drowned out everything else. Ladders led up to the final platforms at the top of the tower. There, nestled among the gears, Riley saw It.<br /> <br /> It was a bizarre amalgamation of nightmare and beauty. Smiling, angelic faces peered out from flesh torn open into ravenous, fang-filled maws. Flesh merged with spokes and gears, twisting and shifting as the seconds ticked by. And Riley could suddenly sense the Azoth blazing like a sun. They raised their gun, prepared to summon a Firestorm to try and burn this creature away, when their access to the Azothic Memory told them what they were looking at. An Archqashmal.<br /> <br /> Riley ran. They raced down the clocktower at a breakneck pace, the stairs appearing to be a lot shorter on the way down than they had on the ascent. When they reached the bottom they began to parse their way through the corridors, finding their way back, when they ran into Elsie stumbling around lost. She told them that Abram was also lost in the halls, but dismissed Riley's idea that they should look for him. This horrified Riley.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't you want to be part of this family?&quot;<br /> <br /> Elsie's reply was a cruel barb, telling Riley that she thought they were the ones who didn't want to be part of the family, since they kept running off to their horse. Hurt and reeling, Riley turned away and went to look for Abram, Elsie reluctantly following along behind them. They found him pretty quickly, only a few corridors away, and Riley then led their throng out of the dream halls and back to the reception area.<br /> <br /> When they stepped out into the room they found the sheriff and his deputies waiting for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T22:52:42-07:00","id":1118842,"title":"","content":"Session 16 - Jailbirds<br /> <br /> The sheriff and his men fumbled for their weapons as the Prometheans came through the door. Everyone froze, a tense standoff, until the sheriff remembered himself and demanded that the throng throw down their weapons. Abram's hand went to his pickaxe, he started to prepare his Pyros to burn and bring the entire building down, but Riley was faster. Their pistol was carefully placed on the ground.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't do it,&quot; they hissed at Abram.<br /> <br /> Once the Prometheans were disarmed, the sheriff's men moved in to arrest them. They were charged with threatening violence against a citizen of Sour Spring. Abram was arrested as the culprit, Riley as his accomplice. No one made any move on Elsie. Instead, the sheriff had a quiet word with her, telling her not to leave town as she was a witness but that as yet no one had suggested that she had anything to do with events. Not long after and she was skipping happily down the road, heading for home, entirely oblivious to the darkening skies.<br /> <br /> Abram and Riley were not quite so blind. They saw the storm coming from the north, an enormous front of dust and debris. The wind was already picking up, filling the air with flying grit. The sheriff's men marched them quickly to the town lock-up, where they split the two of them up. Riley went into an overcrowded cell with half a dozen black men, Abram into a cell with a lone, scraggly-looking white man.<br /> <br /> Riley attempted to talk to the other prisoners. They tried at first to talk about the dreams, but once again they were laughed down by people apparently unprepared to admit that the recurring nightmares were important. Then they tried to muster interest in a jailbreak, but the men were all local and didn't like the sound of being on the run. Finally, they asked about Malik. One of the prisoners, a man who had apparently been arrested only a few hours before for drinking, recognised the description. He'd gone West, Riley was told, not following the road or train. This was about three weeks back.<br /> <br /> Abram, meanwhile, began working at loosening the bars on their cell. A brief protest from their fellow prisoner was shut down by a blunt threat. He had pried two bars loose, creating enough space to fit through. Then, he carefully replaced the bars and prepared for sleep.<br /> <br /> That night, as the Prometheans slept, they found themselves in what looked like a medieval dungeon as they entered the nightmare once again. The sheriff appeared, torch in one hand, keys in the other, and began to unlock the cells. He told the prisoners to gather their weapons, for the hunt was about to begin. They rushed out, part of a mob clamouring for arms. Abram snatched up his pickaxe, Riley got their hands on a shotgun. They stepped out onto the streets of Sour Springs to find it beset by the storm. In the howling wind and dust it was easy for them to quietly separate from the sheriff's gang and make their own way in the dream.<br /> <br /> The storm seemed to be effecting the dreamscape sporadically, occasionally blasting away and making navigation almost impossible, then vanishing in an instant, restoring the dream to its normal state. Abram and Riley picked their way through, making their way to Peter's home to fulfill their promise to protect him. They found him cowering, alone. When asked about his wife, he said she had gone elsewhere to hide. They told him that they thought they had found a way to end the nightmare entirely, but they would have to leave him on his own. It took a bit of wheedling from Riley, but he eventually agreed. Before they left, Riley remembered the conversation they had witnessed between Mikael and the fat man, and asked Peter if he knew the name &quot;Gant&quot;. Peter told them that it was probably Belladonna Gant, the closest person the town had to a doctor.<br /> <br /> They left Peter to go and explore the wealthy estate they had visited earlier that day, where they had seen Mikael for the first time. They found their way there only due to Riley's almost supernatural skill at navigation, the storm had rendered the nightmare even more confusing than normal. When they arrived, everything was still. The building was a gutted ruin, filled with the offal of a pile of dismembered bodies, the house's second floor torn almost entirely out to make it little more than a ruined shell. Riley and Abram glanced at one another. They'd found the lair of one of the beasts.<br /> <br /> They went inside to investigate. While they were in there, they heard heavy footsteps approaching, and went to hide. The massive arm of the largest of the three beasts, the bloated beast whose lupine features were almost obscured under its bodily fat, reached around the edge of a large gap in the wall. It hauled itself into view, filling the interior with the stench of its bodily musk. It looked around, but saw no sign of the Prometheans. Instead it seated itself in a pit of its own filth and began to scoop up body parts from the pile for it, shovelling them into its mouth. Riley glimpsed the head of the building's maid among the carnage. While it was occupied, the two of them were able to steal away.<br /> <br /> In high spirits because they had confirmed the identity of one of the beasts, the two of them headed back across town to the Green Plains Bank. They were about to go in and explore to see if there was any sign of an athanor in the dream, but Abram spotted the smallest, pale beast lurking in the building's shadow. He told Riley to run inside while he distracted it.<br /> <br /> Riley made a sprint for the building, hearing the beast howling in flame as Abram bombarded it with fire. They didn't look back. They rushed inside, and everything went very quiet. The bank was pretty similar on the inside, and they couldn't find anything of note. They went back outside, to find the charred remains of Abram and the pale beast fused together in the middle of the street. Then they heard the approaching footsteps of the elder beast, and ran.<br /> <br /> Elsie woke in the early hours of the morning. She had spent the dream hiding away, and woke up feeling both refreshed and itchy. The black blizzard still raged outside, and dust was seeping into the unsealed building. It covered her skin and clothes. She spent a few minutes petulantly kicking at it for ruining her momentary good mood, and then walked over to feed Baby, but the infant didn't want to eat. Sulking, Elsie hauled the child onto her back and stepped out into the dust storm, fumbling her way through the streets to find the corner store.<br /> <br /> When Abram woke he stepped out through the gap he had made in the bars and went to sit outside Riley's cell. There, to while away the hours of the night, Riley traced words in the dust to help Abram learn how to read.<br /> <br /> Elsie was back in the streets, heading for Mike's Roadhouse. She had a bag on her back, slung next to Baby, packed full of utensils and plates she had looted from the store. It hadn't even taken much effort to force the door open. She intended to take them to Mike and use them for a romantic dinner. That was when she sensed a presence looming over her.<br /> <br /> She looked up, into the distended jaws of Typhoeus. His voice cut through the storm, a gloating, liquid wave of sound.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've been looking for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elsie smiled, always happy to be the centre of attention. &quot;Hello honey!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:36:22-07:00","id":1118874,"title":"","content":"Perfect best ap ever really just so amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T06:42:51-07:00","id":1119238,"title":"","content":"Hahaha, cheers man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think it quite measures up to the likes of the Seventh Seal AP over in the Werewolf forums myself, I just don't have the time or memory to write out our sessions to anywhere near that level of quality. I'm glad you're enjoying what I do put up though.<br /> <br /> Also everyone should read the Seventh Seal. Seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 07-22-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:31:27-07:00","id":1125789,"title":"","content":"Session 17 - Answers<br /> <br /> Elsie waited calmly for Typhoeus to stop shouting. It was some nonsense about her lying to him, running away, trying to trick him. She was just pleased that he'd cared enough to seek her out. When he was done she cuddled closer to him, using his body to shield herself from the storm, and told him the truth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh honey, I didn't want to run. It was Riley. They set everything on fire, and I had to get away from the fire. I didn't want to leave. I couldn't stop them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The enormous sublimati seemed taken aback by that. For all of his immense strength, he seemed unable to overcome the full force of Elsie's indomitable personality. She demanded he follow back to her home and proudly led the way back down the main street, battling the wind and dust.<br /> <br /> Terah did not take the arrival of the titanic monster well. The horse screamed and panicked, trying to pull itself free from its post and escape the small shelter in the back yard of the building. Elsie walked over and calmly untied it, letting the noisy creature run off into the storm. With peace and quiet restored, she had Typhoeus lie his bulk down so that he was almost covered by the roof of the rear porch. She sat down next to him, wearing her gas mask, and placed Baby between them. Over the next few hours she gossiped and chatted happily at him, occasionally inquiring into his past and storing the details away for later. At last she went to go and prepare a meal, but Typhoeus refused the food, instead, he asked for her arm.<br /> <br /> Elsie weighed it up, and recalled that she had read magazines that told her wives should be willing to sacrifice anything for their husbands. If she wanted to keep Typhoeus with her, this seemed like a good place to start. She held out her hand, and Typhoeus took the whole length in his mouth. She then felt repeated stabbing, tearing pains running up and down the limb. When Typhoeus allow her to remove it, long strips and chunks of flesh had been torn away. Elsie cooed and beamed down at the damage, feeling a happy warmth in her stomach at the thought of having pleased her man.<br /> <br /> Across town, Riley and Abram had broken out of their cells, beaten two deputies unconscious, retrieved their gear (and collected some new gear from the deputies, including a badge and a pair of revolvers), and escaped into the storm. They were intent on locating the home of Belladonna Gant, but they quickly became lost in the Black Blizzard. When they felt their throats begin to close, unable to cope with the dust, they stumbled up to the nearest door hammered at it until it opened. They found themselves in Mike's Roadhouse. They told Mike that they were looking for Elsie, that she was missing. He was curiously unresponsive to that, instead shrugging and leading them down into the speakeasy. An older man they had never met before was sitting in the company of several young men, all of them wearing dirty workmen's uniforms.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans stayed a few hours, keeping up the cover by asking the men if they knew where Elsie was. They didn't, but the older man said he'd be happy to help. He was quite interested in meeting the young woman again, too. When they asked if they could wait out the storm in the Roadhouse, Mike told them that they would need to pay for a room. Rather than do that, they instead waited until they felt like they had recovered somewhat and plunged back out into the storm.<br /> <br /> This time they were able to reach Belladonna's house. She was clearly expecting people to come to her during the storm, when they hammered on the door of her modest little townhouse it opened immediately, and they stumbled into a living room where a medical valise was already set up on the central table. Before Belladonna could do more than close the door behind them, however, Riley had drawn a gun on her and demanded answers. They wanted to know everything she knew about the dream, about the wolf-monsters, about why the nightmares were happening and what her role in it all was.<br /> <br /> Belladonna appeared calm, even confident, in the face of the drawn weapon. She asked them to please put the weapon away, and in return she would tell them everything she knew. Somewhat reluctantly, Riley complied.<br /> <br /> Belladonna explained that she had served as a nurse in the great war. In the midst of the battles she saw a man be shot half a dozen times in the chest and keep moving, pus flowing from his wounds in place of blood. The sight set her on a path that led to her discovering alchemical secrets, which she delved into in the hope of finding better ways to treat the sick and injured. Over the years she fell into the company of two other alchemists, the man named Mikael and his associate, a railroad baron named Boris Trammel (the Prometheans assumed this was the fat man in the opulent house they had spied on earlier). They studied and experimented together for years, settling down in Sour Springs, trying to discover new ways to heal and extend natural life. Belladonna always knew the others were in it for more selfish reasons than herself, but figured it didn't matter so long as it would help other people.<br /> <br /> Then, one day, they encountered a creature like the one she had seen in the trenches. It was immediately apparent that its body was filled with alchemical power. Boris and Mikael captured the creature, intending to experiment on it. Belladonna objected, but she couldn't overrule the other two. Instead she split from them, continuing her own research on her own. The night of the creature's capture, however, was when the nightmares began.<br /> <br /> Her own knowledge of the nightmares were limited. To her they were strange visions of blood and fire. She had tried to restrain herself from fighting after she found out that others were experiencing the nightmares as her prey, but fools sometimes sought her out and attacked her. Most nights, however, she simply sought to hide.<br /> <br /> Riley and Abram decided to divulge to Belladonna that they, too, were Prometheans, creatures like the one she had described. Riley asked her to describe the Promethean Mikael and Boris had captured, and was relieved to hear that it had appeared as a young woman. They found out that Mikael had a house down near the bank, and suddenly the Azothic Resonance they had sensed there began to make sense.<br /> <br /> Riley asked for permission to look at Belladonna's books. She refused at first, not wanting to trust her books to strangers, but Abram offered up some of his Pyros to her in return. It was an offer she couldn't refuse. She carefully extracted some of his vital fluids with her medical equipment as Riley poured over the books. Riley couldn't discern anything useful from the books, but Abram did get Belladonna to agree to help in any way she could. She was not interested in fighting, but she was willing to be on hand to tend to them if they were injured rescuing their fellow Promethean.<br /> <br /> The storm still raged outside. They didn't know where Elsie was. But the two Prometheans resolved that they couldn't stand to let one of their kind suffer much longer. They began preparations to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:10:37-07:00","id":1125984,"title":"","content":"Elsie doesn't disappoint in making everything uncomfortable. Your player is on a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T13:04:58-07:00","id":1126005,"title":"","content":"Is Baby protected from the Black Blizzard in that scene? Also Elsie is Cray-cray.<br /> <br /> I see another potential Promethean is getting introduced. Might this be a Character Swap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:51:47-07:00","id":1126120,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1125984#post1125984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elsie doesn't disappoint in making everything uncomfortable. Your player is on a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is real talent there, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1126005#post1126005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Baby protected from the Black Blizzard in that scene? Also Elsie is Cray-cray.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something going on with Baby that the players know about, but the characters don't. I haven't been including it in the write-ups. I'm happy to spoil the revelation, it can't possibly stay a secret for that much longer, or I can hold off until the characters know and reveal it in the write-up. Up to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1126005#post1126005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see another potential Promethean is getting introduced. Might this be a Character Swap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a character swap. Everyone is having a great deal of fun with their characters. We are planning on having a long talk at the start of the next session to work out how the group dynamic will work if Elsie continues down this path though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T21:34:36-07:00","id":1128707,"title":"","content":"Session 18 - Sleeping with the Beasts<br /> <br /> The storm continued to rage throughout the day. Elsie snuggled into Typhoeus's side and, when the wind allowed it, babbled at him about their future. She was able to worm out of him a few insights about what he wanted, and at the top of the list was children. That made her happy. Five, six years from now, she could picture them living together, eleven or twelve offspring swarming all over the place.<br /> <br /> In Belladonna's home, Abram was trying to work through her motives. He had encountered no genuinely selfless humans in his life, so he was suspicious and confused. He understood sacrifice and struggle when it came with a reward, but Belladonna denied that was why she wanted to help people. He understood wanting to help those in your family, and he understood helping those who could be of use to you, but Belladonna had claimed she tried to help people she had never met who would be of no help to her in return. In the war she apparently even cared for the enemy at times. Riley had an easier time grasping the concept, but even they weren't able to make the idea make much more sense to Abram.<br /> <br /> The two of them decided to stay with Belladonna for the night, and attempt to rescue the imprisoned Promethean the next morning. That night, when they slept, they found themselves in what appeared to be a natural cave. The smallest of the three wolf-beasts, the pale one they knew to be Belladonna, was there with them. Backed into a corner, it attacked. Riley ran, sprinting for the exit, while Abram held his ground. The beast bore him to the ground, but in a straight fight Abram's superhuman strength proved to his advantage. He slammed the head of his pickaxe into its stomach again and again. Then, raked by tooth and claw, he kicked the creature to the floor and broke its back with a final blow.<br /> <br /> Elsie had appeared in the nightmare alongside Typhoeus. She convinced him to show his devotion to her by bringing her the head, or heads, of the creature Riley had seen in the clocktower. They set off together, Typhoeus bearing Elsie on her back. When they reached the base of the clocktower they heard howling, and saw the two remaining beasts of the dream approaching together as if to protect the tower. Typhoeus loomed over the bestial creatures. He picked the largest beast up by its neck before it had a chance to create and tore it in two. The elder beast showed no fear at this. Its jaws yawned wide and a stream of corrosive bile poured out, spilling over Typhoeus and Elsie. Elsie felt it bubble and burn its way through her skin, dissolving her, but she lived just long enough to witness Typhoeus bite off the head of the second beast.<br /> <br /> Riley used the dream as an opportunity to scout out the ground ahead of tomorrow's events. They found Mikael's home. Unlike the lairs of the other two beasts, it was strangely normal in the dream. The house itself was blandly sterile and bereft of personal effects. After a few minutes' search they located an entrance on the outside of the house that looked like it would open into a coal cellar or basement. Instead they found a lab, overgrown with pulsating living flesh, lumps of the stuff arrayed on each of the room's three tables and interconnected with rubber pipes and tubes. Riley stared at the sight in horror, hoping that this wasn't what the Promethean captive had become. They explored a little further and found that a curtain at the back of the room opened into a dark pit several metres deep. A winch and cable allowed them to pull up the iron coffin that lay in its depths. When the coffin reached the top, however, a coruscating bolt of flux-like energy blasted out of it and struck Riley in the chest. The next thing they knew, they were waking up.<br /> <br /> With gas masks borrowed from Belladonna, Riley and Abram set out to find Mikael's home. They battled their way through the storm, managing to stick to the route. As they were setting off, Elsie asked Typhoeus to help her locate her friends. She told him that he wasn't to eat Riley, or Abram, they were her friends and belonged to her and even if Riley had separated them before, they weren't to be harmed. Typhoeus appeared to agree to this, on the condition that he still be allowed to taste each of them in turn. Elsie was at first a little insulted that her flesh wasn't enough, but Typhoeus claimed that he didn't want to wear her out by constant feedings. Her pride mollified, Elsie allowed him to lead the way. They talked about the night before on the way, but Typhoeus hadn't been able to get into the Clocktower from the outside. He had contented himself by preying on the townsfolk.<br /> <br /> Abram and Riley had found the building and were standing outside when they heard the heavy tread of massive footsteps. Moments later, Elsie walked into view. Then, before the others could speak, two massive arms settled onto the ground on either side of her, and Typhoeus's head came down to leer at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-28-2017, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T22:15:03-07:00","id":1141319,"title":"","content":"Session 19 - The Family Grows<br /> <br /> Riley's reaction to seeing Typhoeus loom out of the dust was immediate and instinctive. &quot;Elsie, run!&quot; They took off, racing away. Elsie stood where she was, sharing an exasperated look with Typhoeus at her friend's ridiculous behaviour. Abram, seeing that Elsie was making no move to get away, and that she was carrying Baby, stood his ground and hefted his pickaxe. And Riley, realising that none of their throng was following, slowed and turned, pulling out their shotgun, and made their way back.<br /> <br /> Once Elsie explained to her dim-witted friends that no, Typhoeus was not going to eat them, he had promised her that he wouldn't, the other two reacted with a mixture of disbelief and curiosity. Abram bellowed over the storm at the Sublimati, demanding to know his intentions, to know how Elsie had hurt her hand, and why he was so willing to let them live. Typhoeus appeared bored with the conversation, but said that he would only dine on them with their permission, and that he intended to form a family with Elsie. He wanted children, and hoped to make them with her.<br /> <br /> During this, Abram and Riley realised that there was something wrong with Baby. The child was lying very still, listless and unmoving, not reacting to the dust settling on their face. Abram asked Elsie if the child was alright, but she refused to let them near it. She surreptitiously checked the child, but they seemed perfectly fine to her eyes.<br /> <br /> Riley was appalled. They turned towards the alchemists' house. The child was dead, that was clear. At least they could still do some good by rescuing the Promethean trapped inside. They checked the inside of Mikael's house and found it clean but barren, devoid of any personal effects, with no sign of the alchemists in sight. They then continued around the side of the building until they found the coal cellar-like entrance they recalled from the dream. By the time they reached it, the others had caught up. Typhoeus loomed overhead, making Riley's skin crawl. Abram asked what he was planning to do, and he looked over at Elsie.<br /> <br /> &quot;Protect her.&quot;<br /> <br /> Abram smashed the door open with his pickaxe, and the Prometheans rushed inside, descending into the room below. Typhoeus, thanks to his enormous size, had to wait outside.<br /> <br /> They found themselves stepping into a laboratory that closely mimicked what Riley had seen in her dreams. Creatures rendered unrecognisable were splayed on each of the room's three long tables. Chemicals bubbled and boiled in beakers and tubes, distilling strange solutions. The very air stank of Pyros, joined with a sharp, chemical smell that pierced straight through the nose to the brain. Hunched over one of the tables, lit by a single gas lamp above their heads, stood Boris and Mikael, turning to face the source of the noise. Boris frowned and stormed towards them, while Mikael laid his hands on a foot-long object not dissimilar to a medieval mace. It was a round, heavy ball of metal on top of a short shaft.<br /> <br /> Boris stormed up to the characters, demanding that they leave, calling them trespassers and criminals and threatening to summon the sheriff. Riley held their ground, and shouted back that they knew what the alchemists were doing, that they had come to rescue the Promethean they were torturing. Boris looked like he was going to respond, but instead he doubled over in a heavy coughing fit. As he straightened he cast something on the ground. A flash of light lit up the dark room, filling the throng's eyes with dazzling colours, and through it they heard Boris's voice booming. &quot;Leave now. Run!&quot;<br /> <br /> Elsie felt an unnatural emotion creeping into her mind, a total, irrational fear of Boris. As the others went for their weapons, Mikael raised up some rubber tubes which made the room hum and shake. Riley shot Boris in his chest, making a bloody ruin of it, but impossibly the alchemist continued to move. Elsie fought down the urge to flee and threw herself at Boris, bearing him to the ground. Baby fell to the ground in the midst of her panicked frenzy, striking the hard stone and rolling beneath a table. She screamed out for Typhoeus, and the entire building shook as his talons carved out a larger opening to the room, big enough for his arms to reach inside. But with her on top of Boris, there was little she could do.<br /> <br /> Abram and Riley moved past the struggling figures to attack Mikael. The tall, slim man quickly swallowed the contents of a clear vial, his skin rippling as Abram advanced. The pickaxe came flying through the air to strike Mikael in the cheek. It was like hitting a steel pole. Mikael's head turned, a small sliver of blood visible through the grey scales covering what had been soft skin a moment before. Riley fired their shotgun again, but in their haste and panic the shot went wide.<br /> <br /> Mikael focussed on Abram. The Prometheans watched the muscles of his throat visibly rearrange themselves, widening his gullet, and he retched a stream of thick black bile onto Abram. The substance was corrosive and burned Abram's skin horribly, coating him from head to toe, though had he not been Tammuz with his own muscles and blood streams already saturated with such bile he knew he would have been far more wounded. Riley ducked past Abram, shooting Mikael in the stomach. He reacted more like a human should after being kicked in the stomach, not being shot with a shotgun at point blank range. Through the tattered remains of his shirt, they could see that his stomach was also now covered in the same dark scales.<br /> <br /> Behind them, Elsie was getting the better of Boris. He had thrown several punches, and she was bleeding from the nose and a split lip, but she had him on the floor with her hands around his throat. She ground herself down against him, excited to feel him struggling for breath. His eyes rolled back into his head at last, and she leapt up and jumped for joy on his chest.<br /> <br /> Mikael dove for cover behind one of the surgical tables. He raised the mace in his hand, and a blast of lightning launched out of it and struck Abram full on. Abram roared, frustrated that his blows couldn't break through Mikael's skin. He followed the alchemist, striking again and again with the pickaxe, each of his blows jarring his arms and unable to break through Mikael's skin. At last, feeling his body coming apart under Mikael's onslaught, Abram released his grip on the Soldier Role he had embraced for so long, diving into Stannum. The ground beneath and around them shook in sympathy as a wasteland flowed out from his body, flux rippling and distorting the world around them. Mikael paled as lightning danced along Abram's arms. He held out his hands, pouring his Pyros into his newfound power, but Mikael threw himself out of the way and the blast instead tore the wall behind him apart.<br /> <br /> Elsie paused in her excited bouncing when she felt movement beneath her feet. She looked down, curious, as a bloody hand burst out from the wound in Boris's chest. She was sent stumbling backwards as the alchemist's bloated form came apart, torn open by something emerging from the inside. It was a human male, an adult, naked and perfectly proportioned. The gore and fluids of Boris's body slipped from his form as if they could find no purchase on his skin. Long, blonde hair cascaded down to his shoulders, and bright blue eyes scanned the room. Elsie stared this new creature, excited. He turned towards Boris's body and snatched something from the broken corpse's pockets, moments before Typhoeus's hand reached down and wrapped around his waist. As quickly as he had come, the beautiful vision vanished, hauled up and into the storm.<br /> <br /> Mikael was backed into a corner. He tried to drive his opponents off by sending fragments of his stony hide blasting out at them, shredding his clothes as spikes and shards tore through them. They found no purchase in the Prometheans' skin, however, as Riley pushed Abram out of the way in time. He was bleeding heavily, his remaining scales scorched by lightning strikes, blood oozing between them after many shotgun blasts. He held his mace above his head, and the air around it hummed with electrical energy. It exploded out, the Pyros-tainted lightning scorching the flesh of each Promethean in the ruin. Elsie and Riley were blackened and burned, and even Abram felt his flesh scream in protest as the energy coursed through him.<br /> <br /> Riley raised their gun in trembling hands, trying to focus on Mikael, but the shot barely winged him as it went past. Elsie backed up, trying to get out of range of another lightning surge. Abram raised his hands to the sky, pouring his Pyros into a final blast. The lightning swirled around him, crackling and leaping as it surged into his chest, before exploding out in a beam of white-hot energy. It sheered through Mikael, tearing his scales and flesh apart, flinging the alchemist across the chamber and leaving him a crumpled, smoking ruin on the ground.<br /> <br /> The Prometheans took a long moment to get their breath back. Both Riley and Elsie were closer to death than they had ever been before, limping and clutching at injured limbs. Abram, the only able-bodied member of the group, moved to the crank mechanism Riley pointed out to him. The same pit, shielded by a simple curtain, lay at the back of the chamber. Riley called down, asking the prisoner to thump twice on the cage if they understood that they were being rescued and promised not to attack them. A long few seconds passed, and then the characters heard two distant thumps.<br /> <br /> Abram worked the winch and hauled an iron coffin up from the depths. They had to search Mikael's body to find the key, heated to the point where it was still painfully hot to touch. It fit the lock, however, and allowed them to open the coffin.<br /> <br /> The being inside was a ruin of a person. Their naked body was covered in deep, surgical wounds, crusted fluids, and weeping sores. They were so thin and emaciated that their gender was impossible to spot without diving between their legs. Their face was largely obscured by matted hair, but it shifted out of the way to show a single brown eye, bloodshot and full of anger. The rest of their face was covered by something like a gas mask, making it impossible for them to talk. They were strapped into the coffin, and Abram hurried to undo the straps while Riley shrugged off their coat. When the straps were undone the Promethean fell forward, landing in Riley's arms as they smoothly wrapped them in the coat. Lifting the prisoner into their arms, Riley carried them back to the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 09-18-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T04:26:28-07:00","id":1141363,"title":"","content":"This is the best ap i love it that fight was perfect i say i wish i was able to make as amazing fights","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T04:29:20-07:00","id":1141365,"title":"","content":"This is the best ap i say this was the best fight I've seen in ap i can't wait to read your werewolf campaign you made me like promethen thanks and i bet your player's thank you to<br /> Ops my bad i thought i had not posted so sorry i didn't see my 1st post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T22:17:38-07:00","id":1141665,"title":"","content":"Haha, cheers buddy. It was pretty dramatic. I got to really cut loose with Mikael as a high Magnitude Alchemist with a Promethean's worth of Pyros at his disposal. Both Riley and Elsie are heavily into Aggravated damage at this point, and even Abram is going to take a while before he's feeling ok again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T20:56:31-07:00","id":1144276,"title":"","content":"Session 20 - You have twins!<br /> <br /> The storm was still raging when the Prometheans returned to the surface. As they set foot on the ground above, however, they felt a massive surge of Azothic energy from the centre of town. There, somehow, they could see the Gothic spire of the Nightmare's town hall, visible through the dust. As they watched the peak of the spire tore apart, revealing the seething, twisted form of the Arch-Qashmal at its heart. The creature flared its wings, its jaws and faces turned to look at them, and it rose from its place within the tower. Then, as they watched, its body and the tower burned away, leaving only the storm. Each of the Prometheans felt Vitriol surge within their chests, and then all trace of the Qashmal vanished.<br /> <br /> A wail caught their attention, and they turned to see that the beautiful man who had emerged from Boris's body was pinned to the ground with one of Typhoeus's claws embedded in his gut. The sublimati was slavering and barely restraining himself from wolfing down the alchemist. He looked in Elsie's direction and begged her to let him eat the man, saying he smelled so, so perfect. For once, no member of the throng had any problems with Elsie's callous disregard for human life. &quot;Eat up,&quot; she said, and Typhoeus began to force the man into his mouth faster than he could chew.<br /> <br /> They took shelter in Mikael's home while Typhoeus ate. They placed the injured Promethean they had rescued in a chair and quickly swept the house again for anything of use. Abram did turn up some bits and pieces, cloth and thread, that he could use as medical supplies. He set to work tending to the Promethean's words. Before he began he had to pry off the mask bound to the captive's face. It appeared to have been soldered or otherwise fused to their flesh, and required him to leverage both his considerable strength and medical knowledge to tear it away without taking most of the face away with it. He succeeded, and was able to remove the mask taking only a fairly minimal amount of skin and tissue with it.<br /> <br /> Once the mask was off, he could finally talk with the Promethean. He set to work bandaging their wounds, and ask for their name.<br /> <br /> &quot;They called me Vessel,&quot; came the response. The voice was soft and very hoarse, with a strong lisp thanks to a mouth of broken and missing teeth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. Urgh. Do you want to have another name?&quot; Abram was more than a little disgusted, but Vessel just shrugged and said they didn't mind it.<br /> <br /> Abram noticed small red-brown flecks of rust fell from Vessel's lips with every word they spoke. At around this point it also became clear that they were a she. He couldn't determine Vessel's lineage, but guessed that she was most likely an Extempore.<br /> <br /> Once Vessel was all patched up, Elsie shooed Abram and Riley out of the room with some reference to &quot;women's business&quot; and told them to make themselves useful. Once they were gone she promptly ignored Vessel, who quietly passed out, and began to examine Baby. She finally saw what the others had been seeing, that Baby was very, very dead, and had been for a while. She sat there for a while. Outside the room, Abram finished clearing the rest of the house of anything useful, swept dust into the house so that he could lie down in his element without being exposed to the storm, and went to sleep. For the first time since arriving in Sour Springs, he didn't dream.<br /> <br /> An hour or so later, Elsie came to a decision. She took the pearl bracelet she wore and all the materials she could gather from the lab in the basement and filled a large bucket with what she could find. She submerged Baby in the materials and poured her Pyros into the infusion. Perhaps, if she could make Baby a Promethean, no one would notice the difference?<br /> <br /> Beneath the surface, Baby's body rippled. The flesh bulged and split. New growths appeared. Then, as she watched, Baby's body tore in two, splitting from the head and right down their spine. The two halves writhed and formed into twisted little bulbs of tentacles and hard chitin, foetus-like faces staring out at her. The two creatures burst from the bucket, hissing and spitting. They retreated towards the other side of the room. For a moment they appeared poised to attack, when a strange calm swept over them. Elsie took her final step from the Pilgrimage, leaving it behind, and asserted her Lordship over the newborn Pandorans.<br /> <br /> By the time the others woke, her new offspring had spun their cocoons and began to mature. Elsie had packed them into her backpack and fallen asleep beside them.<br /> <br /> Abram was the first to wake, but found that Vessel had risen before him. She had found Mikael's store of fresh water and was gently bathing her arms and face, washing away the filth and stains from her time in captivity. She was still thin to the point of being skeletal, but all of her visible cuts and wounds Abram hadn't yet bandaged had closed over and healed, leaving only scars to show where they had been. When asked, she said the lightning had healed her, and held a hand out to Abram. He took it, and energy poured from her into him, causing his own burns and cuts from the fight with Mikael to heal. He recognised it as an Alembic of the Electrification Transmutation, and thanked her for sparing the energy.<br /> <br /> The throng then split. Abram had decided to loot the now-abandoned General Store under cover of the Black Blizzard. He sent Riley back to the house where they'd been staying, to secure their belongings, as he knew Riley wouldn't approve. Then, accompanied by Elsie, Typhoeus, and Vessel, he led the way through the storm to the store. He forced the door easily and soon his arms were filled with everything that could possibly be of use.<br /> <br /> As he worked, he and Elsie talked. By their reckoning, with the alchemists and Qashmal gone, there was no reason they could not now set themselves up as lords of Sour Springs. If nothing else, the town owed them for their service. Once they had delivered their new belongings back to their lodgings, they decided that they would head across to the local bank and relieve it of everything inside its vaults. Elsie profusely agreed with Abram, even egging him on. Why not just drive out the ungrateful humans, those who had scorned them while they sought to end the Nightmare? Sour Springs could become their own private sanctuary in the wasteland, with only enough humans left to feed Typhoeus. This... Abram was less sure of, but he wasn't as opposed to the idea as he once might have been. Typhoeus had proven himself an ally, after all, far more so than any human in town.<br /> <br /> They made the walk back up the street towards their abandoned home, ugly thoughts swirling in Abram's mind in a perfect reflection of the storm outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T21:00:23-07:00","id":1144278,"title":"","content":"Not a long session this week (we started about an hour late), and most of this session was taken up by just a couple of conversations. Still, always good to have a bit of a palate cleanser after an intense fight like last week. Even if said palate cleanser tastes of Pandoran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T03:07:44-07:00","id":1144326,"title":"","content":"Well, this is going downhill fast, mood-wise.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say it isn't a good or intriguing game. It just jumped from &quot;disturbing&quot; to &quot;villain show, act 1?&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:10:03-07:00","id":1144389,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Riley's player shouldn't miss sessions. They really are the only moral grounding the throng has <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm somewhat optimistic that this plunge towards the darkside is setting up a redemption arc somewhere down the line, but things will undoubtedly get quite dark between now and then.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, that vision of Sour Springs as a Pandoran-infested hellhole ruled by the throng is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T22:57:17-07:00","id":1146572,"title":"","content":"Session 21 - One Bites The Dust<br /> <br /> Riley had returned to the hovel and gathered together the throng's belongings when Elsie and Abram arrived on the doorstop, Vessel and Typhoeus in tow. They were carrying what looked like half the contents of the general store and talking excitedly about robbing a bank. Riley was appalled. Their first priority should be finding Terah, he was missing and must have run off in the storm. Elsie found the idea boring and refused to contribute, which angered Riley. They stormed off to search for their horse, giving Elsie the privacy she needed to tend to her chrysalis-form Pandorans. She could see faint shadows moving within their cocoons, floating in liquid. Satisfied, Elsie returned them to the pack, eager for them to be born.<br /> <br /> For two days, Riley mounted expeditions out into the storm, and Elsie resolutely refused to help. The Black Blizzard showed no sign of abating, and the Prometheans realised that it would likely stay until Typhoeus left town. Entreaties to Elsie to find some way to persuade the Sublimati to move on fell on deaf ears. At last, after another failed search for Terah, tensions came to a head. Riley and Elsie started to argue over Elsie being selfish, while she accused Riley of being an idiot for spending so much effort on a dumb animal. Riley called Elsie a monster, who didn't even care enough about her child to bury them after they had died. Elsie retorted, smugly, that her children would be better off than Riley.<br /> <br /> &quot;At least they have a father.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reference to Malik was enough. Riley snapped. They swung at Elsie. Their fist struck her in the temple. There was a loud crack, Riley left something give way beneath their fist. Elsie crumpled to the ground.<br /> <br /> Shock turned to horror. Riley had forgotten, in the heat of the moment, that Elsie had come out of the fight with the alchemists with the worst injuries of any of the throng.<br /> <br /> Riley's survival instincts had them moving, running for the back of the building, while their mind still grappled with what had happened. Then Typhoeus's roar sounded out, drowning all other thoughts away. Claws tore open the front of the building, shattering wooden beams. Abram dove for his pack, reaching for his weapon, but Typhoeus smashed past him without paying him any attention. Riley vaulted the fence at the back of the building and started to race down the street. They could feel the Sublimati closing on them, the creature's long, loping strides closing the gap in seconds. They were reaching for their revolver when the breath was smashed from their body. They felt ribs splinter, their arm break, a cloud of ephemera bursting from the massive wounds opening all down their right side. They were sent flying down the street to lie gasping in the middle of the road.<br /> <br /> The storm swirled around them, slowly parting as Typhoeus advanced on them. The Sublimati's eyes blazed with hate and anger. Riley raised their revolver, defiant, and poured their Pyros into it. They pulled the trigger, calling a Firestorm into being. The burning, coursing energies exploded out the barrel of the gun with a light so brilliant it was as if a sun had been called into being. Riley felt their skin peel and burn in the light of its energies. A new wind roared into being, blasting the swirling dust away and revealing the length of the street. It was strong enough to lift Typhoeus from his feet and bowl him away from Riley, smashing a house into kindling. When the Sublimati staggered to his feet he was swinging wildly, roaring in pain as the winds hammered him again and again like fists. Riley realised that he'd been rendered blind by the light.<br /> <br /> They turned and ran, staggering through the streets. They could feel the dust clawing at their throat, and they walked with their remaining good hand to the massive wound in their side hoping to prevent the pulped mass within from falling out. At last, they heard something that gave them hope. The sound of hooves, racing towards them. Terah emerged from the dust. Without questioning how he had come to be there, Riley clambered into the saddle and set their horse racing out of town.<br /> <br /> Back in the hovel, Vessel and Abram raced for the exits, trying to escape the firestorm. Elsie's body was left where she lay, but Abram made sure to grab Elsie's pack before he left. The building they'd taken shelter in for the length of their stay in Sour Springs was now a ruin, the few homely touches Elsie had made were now covered in dust as the storm poured in.<br /> <br /> The storm ended, abruptly, on the outskirts of town. Riley didn't let Terah slow until they were miles south, and the storm had receded to a dark smudge befouling the horizon. The horse's flanks were heaving, covered in sweat, and Riley realised that they had no supplies, no food, and no water. They rose in the saddle, scanning the horizon as the sun slowly set. A pale sliver of smoke was just barely visible ahead. They pressed forward, hoping against hope for sanctuary.<br /> <br /> And Elsie, when she opened her eyes, found herself in a vast underground cavern. People thronged around her. She rose to her feet, looking around suspiciously, as an urge came to her from the well of her Azothic Memory.<br /> <br /> <i>Drink from the river.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T23:05:56-07:00","id":1146573,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy. So that was another very short session (we started late again), but boy did it make up for that fact by going in a completely different direction to what I was expecting.<br /> <br /> Neither Riley nor their player realised how badly injured Elsie was when they threw that punch, which was just... just amazing to watch. All the horror and guilt Riley felt afterwards was basically perfectly mirrored by their player, which was really entertaining to the rest of us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:35:34-07:00","id":1149307,"title":"","content":"Session 22 - Enter the Thunderdome<br /> <br /> Abram tried to rouse Elsie, without success. The storm surged into their shattered household, and soon he couldn't make out the closest walls. He rose and tried to find Vessel and spotted her fleeing, heading away from the direction Riley and Typhoeus had gone in. He stood there a moment, unable to decide what to do, and then moved to go after Riley.<br /> <br /> He stumbled through the storm and heard the roar as the Firestorm was unleashed. The winds blasted the dust away, creating a strange bubble, an eye within the black blizzard. He couldn't see Riley anywhere, but he could see Typhoeus as the enormous Sublimati was battered from building to building, blinded by the strange, pulsing lights that flared within the eye. Typhoeus was swinging blindly, and gave no response to Abram's efforts to get him to calm down. Abram grit his teeth and poured his Pyros into his Electrification Alembics. Lightning crackled and crawled across his skin, burning in his eyes and pooling in his wounds.<br /> <br /> He stepped into the Firestorm.<br /> <br /> Typhoeus didn't notice his approach, didn't realise he was under attack until the pickaxe smashed into his chest. His thick, chitinous hide turned the blow, for all its inhuman strength, into little more than a flesh wound. He lashed out, claws raking across Abram's own torso. Bile spilled across the street. Abram pulled back and raised his hands over his head. A sheet of lightning struck his hands and poured from his chest, the energies burning into Typhoeus. The clap of thunder was deafeningly loud. When Abram could see again, Typhoeus was hunched and shaking, his muscles spasming. An enormous burn dominated the Sublimati's forearms, where he'd raised them to ward off the blow.<br /> <br /> A small cheeping sound distracted Abram for a second, and he looked down to see a small feathered head poking out from the ruin of his chest. The canary's feathers were on end, small bolts of electricity bouncing between them. Its eyes were fixed firmly on Typhoeus. It cried out a warning, and Abram threw himself back just in time. A wave of corrosive acid spilled across the ground where he'd been standing, vomited up by the Sublimati. Abram called up another Arc, and this time watched as it seemed to channel itself through the head of his canary. The bird's body was bristling and its eyes filled with rage.<br /> <br /> The blind Sublimati flailed, its wild blows filling the space around it with thrashing limbs. Abram was battered and thrown, feeling ribs break and muscles tear. Thunder sounded again and again as he responded by pouring lightning into Typhoeus. A single almighty blast hurled the creature clear, but it was back on its feet and charging before Abram could get to safety. All around them the Firestorm raged, Abram keeping himself grounded only through his prodigious strength, his vision swimming from the blinding lights.<br /> <br /> A claw came swinging out of nowhere. Abram raised his arm to stop it, and felt each of its bones shatter under the blow. He twisted and sent a bolt of lightning up through the offending limb, heard Typhoeus's unearthly howl of pain in response. Lightning was crawling and creeping through the Sublimati's skin, frying it from the inside. The eye of the storm smelled of burning meat mixed with the sharply chemical sent of the duelling monsters' acidic blood. Typhoeus's umbilical cord whipped up, curling around Abram's leg, but before it could snatch him from his feet he grasped it with his hands and burned it from Typhoeus's body.<br /> <br /> Abram saw the rage in Typhoeus's eyes. The creature pulled itself up to its full height, towering over the broken buildings around them. It took a step forward, claws raised above its head. And there it froze. Abram watched as the massive beast teetered and toppled, collapsing at his feet. He leapt back, waiting for an attack, but none came.<br /> <br /> Typhoeus was dead.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> The crowds of the dead parted around Elsie as she walked. Every now and again she heard whispered voices, some sounding afraid, others accusing. Words like &quot;Murderer&quot; floated by on the edge of hearing. She didn't pay them any attention, after determining that they were all just dead humans. Her Azothic Memory told her what she needed to do to get back to life. Who cared about the opinions of dead humans? It wasn't like they were going to get a second chance.<br /> <br /> Then a figure stepped from the crowd. She vaguely recognised his face. Or rather, what was left of it. It was a teenage boy, his features smashed and bloodied, blood and bone and shattered cartilage breaking through his skin. She tried to place him as he grabbed her hands and started to pull her along, too lost in thought to resist. At last, she worked it out. He was the son of the manager of Sour Springs' general store. She remembered doing this to him.<br /> <br /> As they reached the edge of the cavern together, a great howl went up across the crowd. Elsie turned to look. It was dark in the cavern, but she could see a swirling mass bearing down on the crowd. It looked not dissimilar to the front of a black blizzard, human faces and limbs forming and collapsing within the storm's mass. She saw it envelop the closest of the dead humans, and then the boy pulled her through an opening and into a much smaller tunnel.<br /> <br /> After a while the boy slowed from a run to a walk. He didn't look at her. When she tried to talk to him, his replies were hard to understand, his broken jaw making it difficult for him to pronounce any words at all. He led her deeper and deeper underground, until the tunnel they were walking down ended abruptly. In front of them was a deep, deep chasm.<br /> <br /> Elsie eyed the boy, wondering if he was going to push her in, when a long, multi-jointed limb raised itself above the edge of the chasm. A creature pulled itself up. It was a pallid, thing, clearly human but pulled and stretched until it was impossibly tall and thin. Its face lacked a nose or ears, and its eyes were just dark pits in its skull-like head. It circled its arms around the boy. &quot;Ah, good boy Ciaran,&quot; it said, stroking the teenager's face, caressing his wounds. &quot;You have done well.&quot;<br /> <br /> The creature introduced itself as a guide. It would bring Elsie to the River of Dust, the closest of the Underworld Rivers. It only had one request. When she drank from it, she would return to life. It only asked that it be there when she drank, so that it might come back with her.<br /> <br /> And Elsie smiled and agreed, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T03:52:53-07:00","id":1149357,"title":"","content":"So... A Geist? Prometheans can't become Sin-Eaters, and I don't think you like Crossover, so this is going to turn out <i>well</i> for the Throng.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:00:44-07:00","id":1149412,"title":"","content":"Time and time again I remember why I love Divine Fire. It lets you make dramatically appropriate weather without making it contrived!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T07:38:31-07:00","id":1149679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1149357#post1149357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... A Geist? Prometheans can't become Sin-Eaters, and I don't think you like Crossover, so this is going to turn out <i>well</i> for the Throng.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not a Geist. Probably just an old, old ghost distorted by its time in the Dead Dominions. Probably. I'm sure everything will be fine.<br /> <br /> Abram's player's reaction was something like, &quot;I just finished killing Typhoeus and now you go and get yourself a new one?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Still after watching an already injured Abram down a Rank 5 Sublimati in single combat, even if it was a blind one, I'm not sure they have anything to worry about. At least, not in terms of threats to them personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T20:30:05-07:00","id":1152100,"title":"","content":"Sessions 23 &amp; 24 - Travels far and wide<br /> <br /> Riley and Terah rode into a small camp set up by the side of the road. There was a family of four seated there, boiling a kettle of water. They rushed to help the visibly battered, injured stranger and their exhausted horse, ushering them into camp, binding their wounds, and feeding them soup. When Riley had recovered the better part of their senses, they thanked the family for their kindness. Their hosts were farmers, a husband and wife who had lost their land, their teenage daughter, and their young son. Riley noted that the daughter always kept her parents between her and Riley, but the son wasn't anywhere near that timid. He offered Riley more and more helpings of soup, and solemnly accepted the jerky Riley gave in return.<br /> <br /> As the night grew dark, the family asked Riley what had happened to them. Riley edged around the question, asking if the family had experienced any problems with their travels. Their faces instantly darkened, and though they tiptoed around their own responses, it was clear to Riley that something traumatic had happened between their daughter and a gang of itinerant workers.<br /> <br /> Riley curled themselves up in their blanket and went to sleep that night. As they rested, their humours aligned with the spiritual essence of the place, regenerating their Pyros in a way that usually only happened when there were spirits nearby.<br /> <br /> Back in Sour Springs, Abram had taken up residence in Boris's home. The largest, most opulent residence in town was seemingly deserted, while their own hovel was ruined, so he and Vessel transported the group's belongings into the building. Abram carried Elsie into the garden behind the house and dug a shallow grave. He placed her body in it, and then searched through her pack for Baby's body. Instead he found two cocoons. He recognised them as Pandorans in their chrysalis form. He threw them to the ground and raised his pickaxe to smash them, when they began to hatch.<br /> <br /> The first cocoon broke open with a single long, pale limb. It scrabbled for purchase on the floor, hauling the rest of the Pandoran's slim body free. He emerged from his shell with a rush of embryonic fluid. He wasn't much larger than an eight year old child, but his limbs were too long for his size and he had a large, domed head that gave him an unearthly, alien appearance. His features were delicate, even beautiful, marred only by a cleft palate and rows of tiny, sharp teeth ringing the inside of its mouth.<br /> <br /> The second cocoon shattered apart as a hulking brute of a creature emerged. She had none of her brother's beauty, only bearing the slightest resemblance to humanity. Her mouth and nose pushed forward out of the ruin of her face to form a snout, and she moved with a loping, rolling motion. The left side of her body was withered and vestigial with many weak, withered legs, her left eye clouded and unseeing, while her right-hand side was overbuilt and heavily muscled with three large, powerful limbs. She roared a challenge and charge at Abram.<br /> <br /> The two Prometheans knew they were in no condition for a fight. They left their belongings behind and fled from Boris's home, outpacing the newborn Pandorans. With the dust storm slowly dying down, they went instead towards Mikael's house across town, to shelter there while they healed.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> In the depths of the Underworld, Elsie followed Ciaran and her Guide. The Guide avoided the larger tunnels, winding her deeper and deeper into the Earth. She lost track of time, and eased her boredom by keeping up a constant stream of chatter at Ciaran. The boy never even looked at her.<br /> <br /> Eventually she heard the sounds of music echoing through the tunnels toward her. The sound was a mixture of drums and horns and stranger instruments she had never heard before, accompanied by singing that didn't sound like it was being produced by any human voices. It took hours before they reached the source of the sound, but her Guide led her inexorably towards it. At last her motley group came upon the facade of a grand mansion, emerging seamlessly from the uneven rock wall on either side of it. A line of flickering torches led up to the front door, which appeared to have been knocked from its hinges some time ago. Her Guide told her that the River of Dust lay on the other side of the Bacchanalia, and led her in.<br /> <br /> The dead did know how to party. Elsie saw a man with a cut throat guzzling wine, red liquid pouring down his front and staining his clothes. She saw a woman with burnt red skin and a dress of swirling ash, dancing in the company of two farmers with greyed, swollen faces. She couldn't help herself, she had to join in with the fun. She danced with a group of emaciated men who moved and talked almost in unison, who begged her to stay and be the life of their party. But her Guide intervened, stating that they had a contract, and led her through the crowds of the dead until she reached the rear of the building. She paused only to steal the dress of ash from the body of the burnt woman, found passed out unconscious near the door, before leaving.<br /> <br /> The River of Dust poured almost up to the very steps of the Bacchanalia. There was a thick haze in the air, like the horizon of the Dust Bowl on a windy day. Elsie looked to her Guide for advice, and the tall spectre bade her drink. She grimaced and made a face at the prospect of swallowing dirt, but she took a goblet she had seized during the party still with some wine inside, and filled it with dust from the river. She drank.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Elsie opened her eyes to find herself lying in a shallow grave, at the back of Boris's home. She got up to look for the others, and found their possessions abandoned inside. She was about to look for her children, when they found her. She recognised them on sight, in spite of their new forms, and held out her hands to beckon them in for a hug. When they didn't respond, instead sizing her up as prey from a distance, she pouted and exerted her Lordship over them. Her daughter positively rushed to greet her, while her son seemed to try and resist the impulse. Eventually though, he had to give in. He came to her for a hug.<br /> <br /> Maisie, she decided would be a good name for a her son. And Algernon for her daughter. She went through the house's cupboards until she had material to make them outfits, and set to work making them fit to take out in public.<br /> <br /> Riley woke up and found the camp abandoned. They looked for the family who had hosted them the night before, but there was no sign of them, nor any sign of where they had gone. The camp itself remained, but the tent had partially collapsed. Riley tried to right it, but found that it was caught on something just beneath the surface of the dust. They pulled it away, and found the first body.<br /> <br /> The family were all there. They had died in each others' arms. They couldn't tell what had killed them, but there were no obvious wounds. It was clear, however, that they had been dead for some time.<br /> <br /> Riley buried the bodies, in proper graves this time, digging with their hands. They considered going south, towards Wakesfield, to pursue the gang that had caused the family so much grief, but they couldn't take any more heartbreak on their own. They needed to find Malik. The last information they'd had said he was going West, so they mounted Terah and struck off into the Wasteland.<br /> <br /> Three days passed, with Riley travelling, Abram healing, and Elsie caring for her new children. Keeping them under control was a constant drain on her Pyros. At last, Abram decided he was strong enough to return for his belongings. He could sense Elsie's Azoth from several blocks away, as he closed in on the building, and knew that she must have returned from death. He reached the front door and knocked.<br /> <br /> The door swung open. Elsie was standing there, wearing a new dress, positively beaming at him. She cradled her daughter in her arms, the animalistic horror halfway hidden in something that approximated a white christening dress. It snapped at him, but quietened when Elsie shushed it. Beside her, wearing a dark suit cut to meet his size, was the pale firstborn Abram had almost destroyed in its cocoon. Abram and Vessel stood there, frozen, as Elsie invited them inside.<br /> <br /> Riley had struck a new road, this one leading north-west. They followed it until they reached Fort Bastion. The decommissioned military base was a squat brick of a building, surrounded by an exterior wall made of a wooden palisade and dried mud. As they were riding up to the gates, a voice with a thick German accent asked them to please stop immediately. There were explosives sewn through the area, and he didn't want them to set anything off. Riley followed the instructions that followed, leading Terah through a careful zig-zag up to the front gates, where she was greeted by an aging man who gave his name as Friedrich who took her to see the others.<br /> <br /> There were four old men manning the fort. They didn't tell Riley what they were doing, but they were able to strike up a conversation and found out that the men had come from Sour Springs. They were all veterans, and they seemed to think that they were protecting their hometown from something by being out here. The day was growing late, and they told Riley that they would need to spend the night. For safety, of course. Riley readily agreed.<br /> <br /> The sun set, and Riley sat by the fire and listened to the men talk. None of them were under sixty, all of them had fought in the Great War, and they had been experienced soldiers before then. But they appeared to be kind, and treated Riley and their injuries with kindness and gentle hands, and found a new bed for them to sleep in. All the men slept in the Fort's Armoury, long-since cleared out, now home only to a small collection of firearms that appeared to be the personal possessions of the assembled men. As it grew late, Michael, the only black man among the group, took up a scoped rifle and walked out into the night to keep watch. Riley followed him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T23:16:50-07:00","id":1154064,"title":"","content":"Session 25 - A knock on the door<br /> <br /> Abram and Elsie had a chat, which basically ended in Abram saying he had no problem with the Pandorans so long as Elsie kept them under control, and Elsie saying she really wanted a car. And hey, they knew who had a car too, so the two of them set off across town to Mike's Roadhouse. When they reached Main Street they spotted the sheriff and his men investigating the remains of their old lodging, and presumably Typhoeus's body as well, but the two Prometheans slipped past in the gathering dusk without incident.<br /> <br /> Once inside, they went down to the speakeasy. There was a small, growing crowd within as the men of Sour Springs took advantage of the end of the Black Blizzard to get their first drinks in days. Elsie cornered Mike and persuaded him to come with her into a back room. A lot of hair twirling and battered eyelashes were involved. Abram followed them in, shut the door behind them, and proceeded to threaten Mike into giving him the car. Mike put up some bluster at first, telling Abram that he of all people should know who he was crossing, but when Abram summoned lightning between his fingers Mike's resistance collapsed.<br /> <br /> When they returned to Boris's house in the car to collect Vessel and Else's children, they found Elsie gone. Instead, seated in the living room, was the man they recognised as John Shepherd. He told them that Riley was in great danger, that the dead did not rest easy at Fort Bastion, and that they needed to go there to help urgently. He had sent Vessel on to continue her Pilgrimage, and he was here to make sure that they did the same. With that said, he got up to leave, but he paused to grab Elsie as he made for the door. His face flickered into an expression of disgust as he looked at her, and he told her that he would strongly consider the knife when she found it. Then he left, leaving Else exasperated and more than a little annoyed at the cryptic comment and resolute refusal to explain what he was talking about.<br /> <br /> Riley, meanwhile, was busy exploring Fort Bastion. They'd discovered that the main fort itself, a place the old men rarely entered, still held some records about its history during the last hundred years, including the several times it had changed hands during the Civil War. They found maps showing a lake to the west and a graveyard to the east. There was nothing obviously supernatural, no indication for why the men were so adamant that they not leave at night, until they reached the Gatehouse. Harrison, the leader of the garrison, seemed like he was going to say something when he saw Riley approach the Gatehouse, but he chose to stay silent. The small room was filled with dust, as if a dust storm had raged inside it, and as Riley sifted through the dust they found dozens of human teeth.<br /> <br /> Something about their find spoke to Riley. They gathered up the teeth and wove them into a necklace as they got ready to sleep, and when they were finished they poured all of their guilt and horror from killing Elsie into the necklace to make a Jovian Athanor. And then they fell asleep.<br /> <br /> Hours later, they woke to the sound of gunshots. One of the men sleeping in the Armoury with them, Mack, bounded upright and raced out of the room. Riley reacted more slowly, but they realised that the Fort was under attack. They grabbed their shotgun and ran out into the night.<br /> <br /> They joined Mack and Michael on the walls. There were six figures down below, advancing down the path to the Fort in lockstep. They were dressed like cowboys in heavy dusters and wide-brimmed hats, firing revolvers and rifles up at the fort's defenders. The old men shot back. With the attackers out in the open, bereft of cover, and illuminated by the flashes of their guns they were easy marks, but bullet after bullet sank into their flesh without causing them to do more than stumble. Riley fired their own gun, winging a man with a rifle, and almost took a bullet between their eyes for their trouble.<br /> <br /> Realising how badly wounded they were, Riley took the form of a Bargheist. The next salvo of shots from the defenders focussed on a single attacker, and Riley saw him crumple to the ground, and then through the ground, until the body had entirely disappeared.<br /> <br /> Harrison was struck by a shot from below. A second later, the head of the attacker blew apart as Michael fired his rifle back. As the attackers drew ever closer, Riley was finally able to see them clearly. They had no eyes, or fingernails, or teeth, or tongues, just gaping holes in their head. Their wounds wept greyish fluid, and they continued to fight until their bodies were ruined beyond all hope of repair.<br /> <br /> Moments later, Mack turned and spotted Riley. His gun swung towards them, and they threw their hands in the air. &quot;I'm on your side!&quot; Riley called out. Mack was frozen, his eyes wide with fear. From the corner of their eye, Riley saw a spark sailing towards the attackers. A moment later, there was an explosion. Mack's head snapped around. The attackers were blown apart. Riley took the distraction as an opportunity to return to their regular body, and slipped away before Mack could confront them. A few more shots sounded, and then the coast was clear.<br /> <br /> Riley confronted Harrison, finding Friedrich tending to his wound, and demanded to know what was happening. Harrison was sheepish, but protested that Riley wouldn't have believed it if they hadn't seen the attack with their own eyes. The attackers were the Madsen Gang, a collection of seven criminals, led by the Outlaw Wild Joseph. Mack, Michael, and Harrison had ambushed and killed the gang back when they served in the army, but when they returned from the Great War they had seen signs that the gang was, impossibly, still at large. They had tracked the outlaws down, finding them without their leader just a few months back, and killed them, only to find that doing so hadn't changed anything. Every couple of nights the outlaws would return, and come hunting for them. The old men, with their friend Friedrich, had retreated to Fort Bastion to keep the gang away from Sour Springs and the innocent civilians there. Now they were just seeing how long they could hold out against the undead outlaws. They didn't stop, and Harrison knew well that eventually they would all be overrun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:04:36-08:00","id":1163464,"title":"","content":"Session 26 - Family Reunion<br /> <br /> Hours after the gun battle finished, Mack, Michael, and Riley were still on the walls. Friedrich had taken Harrison to lie down and tend to his bullet wound. Mack didn't broach the subject of Riley's shapeshifting during the fight, and Riley assumed that he was waiting until they were alone to bring it up. They didn't get the chance. During the twilight before dawn, Riley heard the sound of an approaching car. When the vehicle drew closer, they were able to make out the features of Abram and Elsie in front seats.<br /> <br /> Riley immediately assumed that the rest of their throng was here to get revenge upon them for Elsie's death. They grabbed Mack and gabbled, &quot;They're here to kill me! You can't let them inside. Don't hurt them.&quot; Mack was bewildered, but Riley's evident desperation made him agree to keep the other Prometheans away. Riley raced for the fort and lurked where they could hear if there was a commotion.<br /> <br /> They didn't have long to wait. The screaming started several minutes later, followed by several gunshots. Riley dashed out in time to see Mack racing for the fort, pushing past them without a word. Michael had thrown himself flat. And still Riley could hear gunshots. They summoned their courage and ran for the walls. There, on the road below, Abram was standing at the edge of the booby trapped stretch in front of the fortress and firing a revolver into the ground seemingly at random. Elsie stood beside him, cradling an abomination in a dress in her arms, a second creature at her feet. Riley recognised them as Pandorans, and realised that Mack and Michael must have been overwhelmed by Pandoran Disquiet.<br /> <br /> Somewhere behind them, Friedrich and Harrison were emerging from the armoury and hurrying to help. Riley screamed at them to stay back. At the sound of their voice, Abram called out. To Riley's surprise, he sounded happy to see them. He said he'd come to help, that they'd heard that Riley was in danger and they were here to make sure they were safe.<br /> <br /> Riley's incredulity only built as the conversation continued. Elsie claimed that she wasn't holding a grudge for being killed, and Abram said that he didn't blame Riley for what had happened. They were a family, they needed to stick together no matter what. As far as Riley could tell, they were both telling the truth. Abram asked if they could enter the fort, but Riley told them that they couldn't bring the Pandorans inside. This seemed to surprise both Abram and Elsie, but they followed Riley's instructions and left Elsie's children in the car.<br /> <br /> They entered the fort to be greeted by rifles pointed at their faces by Harrison and Friedrich, but Riley managed to calm the situation. The three Prometheans withdrew from the humans to talk among themselves. Riley infused their humours with their own memories, and shared their Essence with the other two to try and convey what they were feeling. The throng watched Riley's memories of travelling with Malik and the persecution the two of them had suffered everywhere they went. Riley tried to explain how important Malik was to them. In the course of activating these Alembics, they delved into their Azothic Memory and discovered that there were Pilgrim Marks in the area, out near the dried-up lake to the west. After some discussion though, the group decided to use their daylight hours to head east and explore an old military graveyard there, to see if there were any spirits or ghosts about.<br /> <br /> Riley told Harrison that they would all be back before nightfall. They decided to travel by car as far as the road would take them. Riley sought to sit as far from the Pandorans as possible, concerned that Abram didn't seem to mind their presence.<br /> <br /> The car didn't take them far, in the end. They'd been driving for a little over an hour when the road grew too rough to drive, and something struck the bottom of the vehicle hard enough to kill it in its tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T23:15:13-08:00","id":1168725,"title":"","content":"Session 27 - The Siege<br /> <br /> The throng hurried back to the fort before nightfall. They spoke with Harrison and the other defenders. Riley was still badly injured, and Abram wanted to stay somewhere safe until they were better. Harrison appeared skeptical at the description of Fort Bastion as &quot;somewhere safe&quot;, but he was happy to allow Abram to join them.<br /> <br /> The siege began.<br /> <br /> For the next month, the throng helped defend the walls. Riley was cloistered away in the armoury, forbidden from joining in the fighting, but they could help by preparing weapons and ammunition. Abram managed to persuade Elsie to help him kill the revenants, and when the attacks came, as they did every three or four nights, they would help the old men drive back the zombies. Some nights Abram would lay an ambush outside the wall, and when the revenants appeared he would descend upon them with pickaxe in hand, slaughtering them on his own. Other times he would take up a shotgun, and Elsie her revolver, and they would help to gun down the revenants before they reached the walls.<br /> <br /> At the month's end, the Fort still stood. Riley had noticed that Matthew appeared to be suffering somewhat from an old wound, and it was becoming increasingly obvious that all of the men bar Harrison were falling subject to Elsie's Disquiet. The throng decided to mount another expedition to the old military graveyard as much as a way to cut the rising tensions as anything.<br /> <br /> They passed the remains of their car on the way. It was a blackened wreck, clearly torched more than a few weeks ago. By the time they reached the graveyard, the sun was setting. The graveyard itself was small and simple, just a few rows of wooden crosses arrayed out from a central open space. Riley called on their Ephemeral Flesh as they entered the graveyard, eager to perceive any ghosts that might be about, and froze.<br /> <br /> Right in front of them, its long fingers intertwined with the base of Abram's skull, was a spectre like nothing they had ever seen. It was stretched and thin, impossibly tall, and they could only see the barest traces of its former humanity among its distended features. It turned to look at them, realised it was being perceived, and Riley watched as it poured itself into Abram's head.<br /> <br /> The puppeteer turned its new skin towards the rest of the throng, and bowed its head to Elsie. &quot;I must thank you for bringing me back in the presence of so-suitable an anchor. This body is perfect for my needs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elsie blinked. The creature turned its attention back to Riley. The moment its eyes moved away from her, Elsie raised her revolver and shot it twice in the back of the head.<br /> <br /> A roar tore from Abram's throat, but before he could react Riley, covered in fur and sprouting claws, slammed into his midsection. He was bowled to the ground. Seconds later, Elsie joined in on the heap, but now she was stroking his face and coaxing a very surprised moan out of him. The ghost riding his body was so stunned by the sudden affection that it reacted too slowly as Riley tapped into the Azothic Memory to discover the secrets of abjuration, calling on memories of love and family to pull the ghost out.<br /> <br /> Abram jerked, and the ghost came pouring out of his mouth. Incorporeal again, it vented its frustration on the only target it could reach. Riley felt the heavy impacts in their side, but returned the favour with tooth and claw. Before the somewhat befuddled eyes of the rest of the throng, they danced back and forth with the ghost, slashing and tearing, until at last the ghost's body began to peel apart into a swarm of leeches. They were carried away on the wind, leaving Riley panting, exhausted, but with the Twilight around them apparently devoid of spirits and spectres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T23:16:45-08:00","id":1168726,"title":"","content":"My apologies on the delay with that write-up, at this point it's probably about two weeks old.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be travelling so I wouldn't expect another recap for about two months, give or take. Early February will likely be the next Promethean session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T23:22:20-07:00","id":1207561,"title":"","content":"Session 28 - From fire we came...<br /> <br /> Riley escorted a dazed and confused Abram away from the graveyard, explaining to him what had happened. Elsie followed along in their wake, only to have Riley round on her and demand what the ghost had meant by thanking her. Elsie denied any involvement, exasperating Riley when it was clear that she was lying, but with Elsie refusing to engage the throng could only walk back towards the fort in stony silence.<br /> <br /> They had been walking for several hours when the western horizon lit up with an orange glow. It was clear to the Prometheans that there must be a massive blaze raging at Fort Bastion to be visible from so far away. They broke into a run and raced across the flats, eating up the distance. They arrived to find a grand crater where the road leading up to the fort had been, and the gates of the fort off their hinges. Flames raged around the gatehouse, and Abram slowed to try and douse them. Riley and Elsie pushed forward and almost tripped over the body of Mack, the fort's tracker, his body riddled with bullet holes. Riley opted to circle the fort to find Terah, while Elsie headed for the main building where she had left her Pandoran children.<br /> <br /> Riley found Terah still tied to a post, eyes rolling and trying to pull away. Michael sat tending to a wounded Friedrich. Riley calmed Terah and ordered the two old men atop the horse, telling them to make their escape. Michael told them that he had seen two revenants enter the fort, but he wasn't sure how many were still around.<br /> <br /> Inside the fort, Elsie came across one of the revenants grappling with her daughter Algernon. She sat back and watched with visible satisfaction as the Pandoran tore the undead creature apart. She was looking around for something to steal, disappointed that the revenant's body and possessions had faded upon death, when Riley burst into the building and pushed past her without a word.<br /> <br /> On the second floor of the fort, Riley found Maisie, the second Pandoran, dispatching a revenant. Maisie's spiked tongue punched in and out of the revenant's skull, leaving the Pandoran with blackened gore streaked across his distended features. Then, he turned his attention to Riley. Riley attempted to push past, but Maisie coiled to strike the moment they came within reach.<br /> <br /> The sound of gunshots from the fort's second floor caught the attention of Abram and Elsie. Elsie, actually inside the building, reached the landing and saw what was going on first. A badly wounded Maisie was struggling to stay on his feet, bleeding from open wounds in his face and fragile chest, opposite Riley who looked similarly close to death. Elsie noted with displeasure that blood was soaking into the suit she'd stitched for Maisie. Just before the Pandoran tensed to leap and finish off Riley, Elsie raised her own pistol and shot him through the head.<br /> <br /> Riley didn't stop to thank Elsie. They turned to push deeper into the fort, hunting for the last of the old men left to defend it. They had only taken a couple of steps, however, when they heard Elsie's gun fire again, and felt a bullet punch in between their shoulder blades. They screamed in rage at this betrayal, falling immediately into Stannum, but they were too wounded to fight. They ran, and Elsie and Algernon gave chase.<br /> <br /> Unlike her peers, who had expended every ounce of energy and Pyros in the fighting with the revenants and the ghost in the graveyard, Elsie was well rested and brimming with energy. She pushed her strength to unnatural levels and ran Riley to the ground. She pushed them down and tore into the flesh of their back, attempting to perform a lacunae and rip out the Vitriol from Riley's body. Riley struggled, and Elsie was only able to snatch a taste before Riley was on their feet and turning, firing their gun into Elsie's chest.<br /> <br /> This was the tableau Abram saw when he caught them, rounding the corner to the sound of Riley's gun. He had a moment to see Elsie staggering back, scarlet blood running down her chest, and barreled towards Riley roaring at them to stop fighting. Riley, frenzied and nearing Torment, saw only another massive foe bearing down on them. They ducked out of the way, straight into the waiting claws of Algernon. The Pandoran's claws bit deep, damaging something vital within Riley, but Abram tore them free from Algernon's grasp before Algernon could finish the job. Riley hung limp in Abram's grasp, struggling to move damaged limbs. They tried to speak, but whatever they were going to say was drowned out by a gunshot. Abram felt Riley stiffen and saw the ephemera flow from the new hole in the side of their head. A lifeless body dropped to the ground.<br /> <br /> Abram turned towards Elsie, grief rising inside him. Before he could act, however, Algernon struck. The Pandoran's target had shifted the minute Riley died. Claws and fangs rent deep furrows in Abram's body, spilling blackened pus and fluids across the ground. Abram struggled and threw off the Pandoran and snatched up his pickaxe. To his right, Elsie pulled the trigger on her gun, then screamed in frustration when she realised it was out of bullets. She threw the weapon at his head, but he ducked out of the way and brought his weapon down on Algernon in the same fluid move. The blade went straight through the small Pandoran, pinning it to the ground. A bubbling wail burst out of Algernon's mouth, and she flailed wildly back at her attacker. A second blow put her in the ground.<br /> <br /> Elsie charged at Abram before he could catch his breath. The two Prometheans, slick in the black and red fluids pouring from their wounds, struggled in the dark. Elsie's nails tore Abram's savage wounds ever wider. He threw her off him and dealt a crushing blow to her chest, leaving her gasping on the ground. Abram raised the pickaxe to finish her off, but he hesitated.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why? Why do this?&quot;<br /> <br /> Elsie smiled, baring reddened teeth up at her throngmate. &quot;I spent so long thinking I needed you, that I needed someone strong. I thought I needed to serve them, so that they would then protect me. But you know what? I don't need you anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Abram brought the pickaxe down. It smashed through Elsie's side, shattering ribs, almost gutting her entirely. But she kept moving. Her fingers found Abram's neck, her nails plunged up through his flesh, and she ripped him open. His enormous body crashed to the ground, shaking the floor beneath her.<br /> <br /> Friedrich and Michael, far away at this point, saw a lone figure emerge from the burning fortress. She was barely standing, drenched head to toe in black and red, and moved like she was dragging her own damaged body by sheer force of will. And she was smiling.<br /> <br /> They didn't turn back again, not until they had driven Terah as far and hard as they could, and that lone figure had disappeared far over the horizon.<br /> <br /> OOC: Ok, so real life events conspired to throw a few spanners in the works with getting this campaign going again. One of the players landed a job overseas during our hiatus, but we had an opportunity to get together one final time over the weekend and work towards a conclusion. Everyone cut a little loose as a result, so... that happened. Not yet sure if this will be the final session or if there may be 1-2 more player sessions to round out the ending a bit more thoroughly, but there's every chance that this will end up being the finale.<br /> <br /> For the record, Elsie walked out of there with aggravated damage filling every health box bar her last. She had full Pyros and Willpower at the session, the only player with any, and she burned all of it over that fight. I'm not sure I can imagine any fight going closer to the wire than that one did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T02:33:20-07:00","id":1207589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1207561#post1207561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOC: Ok, so real life events conspired to throw a few spanners in the works with getting this campaign going again. One of the players landed a job overseas during our hiatus, but we had an opportunity to get together one final time over the weekend and work towards a conclusion. Everyone cut a little loose as a result, so... that happened. Not yet sure if this will be the final session or if there may be 1-2 more player sessions to round out the ending a bit more thoroughly, but there's every chance that this will end up being the finale.<br /> <br /> For the record, Elsie walked out of there with aggravated damage filling every health box bar her last. She had full Pyros and Willpower at the session, the only player with any, and she burned all of it over that fight. I'm not sure I can imagine any fight going closer to the wire than that one did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did Abram or Riley die before, I forget? They might be back up to finish the fight if so.<br /> <br /> That <i>was</i> a pretty rank betrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:03:21-07:00","id":1207639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1207589#post1207589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Abram or Riley die before, I forget? They might be back up to finish the fight if so.<br /> <br /> That <i>was</i> a pretty rank betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lesson 1: Don't keep Centimani around in your throng.<br /> <br /> Neither Abram nor Riley have died previously, so they have both been plunged into the Underworld. I'll try and get a chance to wrap up the story from their perspectives, but I think it's looking like Abram might be one of those Prometheans who never make it back from the River. Riley's player and I will try to sort something out, but if we don't get the opportunity then it may be that fire took the fort and the bodies of the Prometheans before they completed their journeys in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Still, even with the imminent end of the campaign, I am very glad my group is ok with betrayal and player vs player fights. This one has been brewing for a while, it was nice to finally play it out and it did not go the way I was expecting. Elsie is easily the weakest member of the throng in a fight, and even with Algernon on her side I wasn't expecting a Rank 1 Pandoran and her to stand up to Abram (mister &quot;I can kill a blind Rank 5 Pandoran&quot; himself). Killing Riley as well was exceptionally impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T08:56:59-07:00","id":1207669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1207639#post1207639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesson 1: Don't keep Centimani around in your throng.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally sound advice. I knew she was trouble what with her general disinterest in others well-being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1055448-it-was-written-in-the-dust-a-promethean-dark-era-actual-play?p=1207639#post1207639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elsie is easily the weakest member of the throng in a fight, and even with Algernon on her side I wasn't expecting a Rank 1 Pandoran and her to stand up to Abram (mister &quot;I can kill a blind Rank 5 Pandoran&quot; himself). Killing Riley as well was exceptionally impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bResources - they matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}